00:36:56.050 --> 00:36:58.040
Now you have in mind the anatomy

00:36:58.070 --> 00:37:02.020
of the hair and the area from which it
grows,  and the stem cells, et cetera.

00:37:02.040 --> 00:37:05.400
The fact that there's  capillary
innervation delivering oxygen and blood

00:37:05.430 --> 00:37:09.800
flow to the stem cells  that give rise
to the hair, and that there are these

00:37:09.830 --> 00:37:14.580
three critical phases of hair growth:
anagen, catagen, and telogen.

00:37:14.610 --> 00:37:17.040
Now, let's talk about the accelerators

00:37:17.070 --> 00:37:20.260
on hair growth and the
brakes on hair growth.

00:37:20.280 --> 00:37:21.960
There are many accelerators on hair

00:37:21.990 --> 00:37:27.880
growth, but the first one that I really
want to underscore is blood flow itself,

00:37:27.910 --> 00:37:31.620
which equates to the delivery
of nutrients and oxygen.

00:37:31.650 --> 00:37:33.360
This is very important,

00:37:33.390 --> 00:37:38.020
and it explains a lot of the treatments
for halting and reversing hair loss.

00:37:38.040 --> 00:37:40.080
For instance, one of the longest standing

00:37:40.110 --> 00:37:44.760
treatments for halting and reversing
hair loss  is so-called minoxidil.

00:37:44.790 --> 00:37:49.300
Minoxidil, sometimes also referred
to by the brand name ROGAINE,

00:37:49.330 --> 00:37:53.170
was actually a drug that was
developed to treat hypertension.

00:37:53.200 --> 00:37:56.000
This is a cardiac drug that lowers blood

00:37:56.030 --> 00:37:59.200
pressure,  and it does
that by causing vasodilation.

00:37:59.230 --> 00:38:00.960
It allows more blood flow,

00:38:00.990 --> 00:38:05.210
not just to the hairs on your scalp,
but to hairs everywhere on your body.

00:38:05.240 --> 00:38:07.040
Indeed, most people don't realize this,

00:38:07.070 --> 00:38:11.640
but minoxidil won't just  slow  the loss
of hair from your scalp,

00:38:11.670 --> 00:38:15.480
it is also effective at slowing
the loss of hair elsewhere in your body.

00:38:15.510 --> 00:38:17.020
How does it do that?

00:38:17.050 --> 00:38:20.080
Well, you now know one
of the major ways it does that.

00:38:20.110 --> 00:38:25.920
It does that by extending the anagen
phase, so it basically makes that phase

00:38:25.950 --> 00:38:30.600
a bit longer, and does it make it
much longer, which is why for most people

00:38:30.630 --> 00:38:34.160
who are losing their hair quickly
or who have already lost their hair,

00:38:34.190 --> 00:38:37.210
minoxidil alone is not going
to be a sufficient treatment.

00:38:37.240 --> 00:38:41.880
However, minoxidil  has been shown to be
effective at slowing rates of hair loss

00:38:41.880 --> 00:38:44.060
in people that are starting
to experience some hair loss.

00:38:44.080 --> 00:38:45.400
I'll get into dosages and things

00:38:45.400 --> 00:38:48.320
of that sort a little bit later,
but right now I just want to really focus

00:38:48.350 --> 00:38:51.120
on the logic of why people would take
this  drug,

00:38:51.150 --> 00:38:56.020
which is lowering hypertension
at all as it relates to hair loss.

00:38:56.050 --> 00:38:57.960
That might seem like crazy until you

00:38:57.990 --> 00:39:01.420
understand the anatomy and the growth
of hairs, which you now do.

00:39:01.440 --> 00:39:02.760
That's what minoxidil is doing.

00:39:02.790 --> 00:39:07.720
It's creating more  blood flow
to the hairs, which because minoxidil

00:39:07.720 --> 00:39:11.040
does have this positive effect,
at least most people would like  to slow

00:39:11.070 --> 00:39:15.880
their rates of hair loss on their scalp
anyway, it tells you that blood flow

00:39:15.910 --> 00:39:19.800
and delivery of oxygen and other
nutrients from the blood is pretty

00:39:19.830 --> 00:39:25.860
critical,  if not very critical, for the
support  of the hair growth cycle itself.

00:39:25.890 --> 00:39:30.240
Now, again, we haven't talked at all about
the sorts of chemicals or the signals

00:39:30.240 --> 00:39:33.900
within the body, such as hormones
that actually direct the growth of hairs.

00:39:33.920 --> 00:39:34.920
Here, we're just talking about

00:39:34.950 --> 00:39:38.040
a mechanical change,
allow more blood flow  to the region,

00:39:38.070 --> 00:39:42.340
and thereby extend the anagen phase, which
is exactly  what happens with minoxidil.

00:39:42.370 --> 00:39:46.640
Now, minoxidil does have other effects,
and this is why dosing of minoxidil

00:39:46.670 --> 00:39:51.100
becomes a little bit complicated and can
be a little bit tricky to troubleshoot.

00:39:51.130 --> 00:39:55.320
It can greatly lower blood pressure
or lower blood pressure just a little bit,

00:39:55.350 --> 00:39:58.900
depending on how sensitive somebody
is to that particular drug.

00:39:58.930 --> 00:40:03.000
Oftentimes physicians will start people
on Minoxidil dosages that are very low.

00:40:03.030 --> 00:40:07.160
Ideally, that would be the case and then
ratchet it up in order to figure out

00:40:07.160 --> 00:40:11.120
where the minimal effective dose  or the
critical threshold is beyond which they

00:40:11.150 --> 00:40:14.400
start experiencing  some pretty
uncomfortable side effects,

00:40:14.430 --> 00:40:18.440
such as swelling of the ankles
or headaches or dizziness.

00:40:18.470 --> 00:40:22.460
These things can happen  with the use
of Rogaine, aka Minoxidil.

00:40:22.490 --> 00:40:27.780
Now, Minoxidil has also been associated
with increases in the hormone prolactin.

00:40:27.810 --> 00:40:31.360
Prolactin is a hormone that's
released  from the pituitary.

00:40:31.390 --> 00:40:36.800
It is a hormone that acts also as a bit
of a neurotransmitter, like many hormones,

00:40:36.830 --> 00:40:41.380
and it tends to be antagonistic
or an opposite to dopamine.

00:40:41.410 --> 00:40:43.560
Dopamine is a neurochemical.

00:40:43.560 --> 00:40:45.000
It's actually a neuromodulator,

00:40:45.000 --> 00:40:48.000
meaning it modulates the activity  of a
bunch  of neural circuits in the brain.

00:40:48.030 --> 00:40:51.480
It also controls the release
of various hormones in the body.

00:40:51.510 --> 00:40:57.000
Dopamine is almost always associated with
states of motivation, pursuit, and drive.

00:40:57.030 --> 00:40:59.240
It has a little bit  of a feel- good

00:40:59.240 --> 00:41:01.080
element to it,
which is why a lot of people think

00:41:01.080 --> 00:41:03.360
dopamine is associated
with reward and pleasure.

00:41:03.390 --> 00:41:06.960
But it's really about energy,
motivation, and drive.

00:41:06.990 --> 00:41:08.800
Dopamine and prolactin are,

00:41:08.800 --> 00:41:10.960
as I mentioned before,
antagonistic to one another.

00:41:10.990 --> 00:41:13.060
They're in sort of a push-pull.

00:41:13.080 --> 00:41:16.120
People who take Minoxidil,
especially if they're very sensitive to it

00:41:16.150 --> 00:41:20.720
or they take dosages that are too high,
will experience increases in prolactin

00:41:20.750 --> 00:41:25.600
that in turn can cause things  like
reductions in libido,

00:41:25.630 --> 00:41:29.280
reductions in overall feelings
of well-being, apathy,

00:41:29.310 --> 00:41:33.600
and in some cases where the elevations
in prolactin are more extreme,

00:41:33.630 --> 00:41:37.400
they can experience, for instance,
increase in male breast tissue

00:41:37.430 --> 00:41:42.320
gynecomastia or even small bits
of milk letdown, things of that sort.

00:41:42.350 --> 00:41:44.320
In women who take Minoxidil,

00:41:44.350 --> 00:41:48.170
the side effects are much like
the ones in experienced in men.

00:41:48.200 --> 00:41:49.160
So there can be swelling,

00:41:49.190 --> 00:41:52.960
edema of the tissues
because if you get too much  vasodilation

00:41:52.990 --> 00:41:56.200
and too, too much lowering of blood
pressure, that's not good.

00:41:56.230 --> 00:41:58.060
Headaches, dizziness and so on.

00:41:58.090 --> 00:42:00.300
Dosing of Minoxidil  is really important.

00:42:00.330 --> 00:42:03.000
If somebody is going to use Minoxidil

00:42:03.030 --> 00:42:07.840
in order to try and slow or reverse hair
loss, again, it mainly is going to be used

00:42:07.850 --> 00:42:10.900
to slow rates of hair loss,
not to actually reverse hair loss.

00:42:10.920 --> 00:42:13.340
The really key thing  is
to get that dosage right.

00:42:13.360 --> 00:42:15.000
The ranges of Minoxidil  that you'll see

00:42:15.030 --> 00:42:18.580
suggested and that people
use out there are vast.

00:42:18.600 --> 00:42:20.480
I should also mention  that there are two

00:42:20.510 --> 00:42:23.680
major routes by which people get
Minoxidil to the hair follicle.

00:42:23.710 --> 00:42:25.800
One is to take it systemically as a pill

00:42:25.800 --> 00:42:27.780
where it goes into the
general circulation.

00:42:27.810 --> 00:42:30.780
The other is to take it
topically as a cream.

00:42:30.810 --> 00:42:33.240
There are prescription  and non-

00:42:33.240 --> 00:42:36.280
prescription forms of Minoxidil
just to further complicate things.

00:42:36.310 --> 00:42:40.520
But the ranges of oral Minoxidil
that you'll see out there and that people

00:42:40.550 --> 00:42:47.900
take range anywhere from 0.25 milligrams
all the way up to five milligrams per day.

00:42:47.920 --> 00:42:48.920
That's an enormous range.

00:42:48.950 --> 00:42:51.500
It's like a 20-fold range.

00:42:51.530 --> 00:42:56.160
The topical Minoxidil  is also
found in various concentrations.

00:42:56.180 --> 00:42:58.280
The typical concentration  is going to be

00:42:58.310 --> 00:43:01.600
a 5% concentration that people
will use once per day.

00:43:01.630 --> 00:43:04.680
Topical treatment with Minoxidil  at 5%

00:43:04.710 --> 00:43:10.120
concentration is thought to just stay
at the scalp,  but we now know that it

00:43:10.120 --> 00:43:13.040
can go systemically,  it can get
into the general bloodstream.

00:43:13.040 --> 00:43:14.520
Why that is should make complete sense

00:43:14.520 --> 00:43:17.160
to you because when you put something
on your scalp, I've already told you

00:43:17.190 --> 00:43:20.680
that these little pits,
these little tubes that go down to those

00:43:20.710 --> 00:43:26.580
bulb regions below the skin  that have
direct access to the blood supply.

00:43:26.600 --> 00:43:27.920
When you massage something  into your

00:43:27.920 --> 00:43:31.600
scalp, it not only has the opportunity
to get into your general circulation,

00:43:31.630 --> 00:43:35.600
it often does,
especially if it's something that's very

00:43:35.630 --> 00:43:39.840
water-soluble and that way can get
into the capillaries and into the general

00:43:39.870 --> 00:43:44.000
bloodstream,  although topical treatments
of which we're going to discuss,

00:43:44.030 --> 00:43:48.840
a number of them today don't tend to get
into the general circulation as robustly

00:43:48.870 --> 00:43:52.700
as taking something
by way of pill or capsule.

00:43:52.730 --> 00:43:55.280
Minoxidil works by way of increasing blood

00:43:55.310 --> 00:43:58.380
flow to the stem cell
niche below the hair.

00:43:58.410 --> 00:44:01.480
The dosage ranges  of the oral Minoxidil

00:44:01.510 --> 00:44:06.300
are tremendous, 0.25 milligrams, all the
way up  to five milligrams once per day.

00:44:06.330 --> 00:44:10.960
The dosage range of the topical solutions
tends to be a little bit more confined.

00:44:10.990 --> 00:44:13.160
Typically, it's a 5% solution  and it's

00:44:13.190 --> 00:44:17.400
recommended that people
use it one time daily, maybe twice daily.

00:44:17.430 --> 00:44:20.800
It's also important, by the way,
if you're going to take this route,

00:44:20.830 --> 00:44:24.320
that you actually leave that solution
on the scalp for 3-5 minutes.

00:44:24.320 --> 00:44:27.440
This is important and should make
complete sense as to why it's important.

00:44:27.440 --> 00:44:28.880
You can't just rub the stuff  into your

00:44:28.880 --> 00:44:31.160
head and then rinse it off
and expect it to be absorbed.

00:44:31.190 --> 00:44:36.200
It actually needs to seep down into those
hair follicles and access the niche.

00:44:36.230 --> 00:44:40.840
How do people arrive  at the
correct dosage for Minoxidil?

00:44:40.870 --> 00:44:44.680
Well, for better or for worse,  really,
in some cases,

00:44:44.710 --> 00:44:50.500
it's accomplished by finding out that you
have an unwanted side effect, like

00:44:50.530 --> 00:44:55.280
dizziness or swelling  of your ankles or
edema or I would hope this wouldn't be

00:44:55.310 --> 00:44:59.460
the case,  but something that suggests
there's hyperprolactinemia.

00:44:59.480 --> 00:45:01.040
You could get a blood test  to measure

00:45:01.070 --> 00:45:05.900
your prolactin or you perhaps notice
a drop in libido or some lethargy.

00:45:05.930 --> 00:45:07.800
These sorts of things that are common

00:45:07.830 --> 00:45:10.980
to reduce levels of dopamine,
increased levels of prolactin.

00:45:11.000 --> 00:45:14.000
I would hope that if people are working
with a physician or if they're not

00:45:14.030 --> 00:45:19.740
in taking Minoxidil, that they would
start  with the lowest possible dose.

00:45:19.770 --> 00:45:23.280
For oral Minoxidil,
that would be 0.25 milligrams and then

00:45:23.290 --> 00:45:27.440
increase it as needed  rather than jumping
in right at five milligrams  because some

00:45:27.440 --> 00:45:30.120
of those side effects,
in particular the fluid  retention

00:45:30.120 --> 00:45:33.240
and the hyper prolactinemia
can be pretty uncomfortable  and can

00:45:33.270 --> 00:45:37.740
disrupt a lot of aspects of life
that most all of us consider desirable.

00:45:37.770 --> 00:45:40.720
We're really focusing right now
on treatments that relate

00:45:40.750 --> 00:45:46.280
to the critical requirement for hair stem
cells to receive  blood flow  in order

00:45:46.310 --> 00:45:50.100
to receive oxygen and nutrients,
to get the hair to grow.

00:45:50.130 --> 00:45:52.400
That's really what Minoxidil is about.

00:45:52.430 --> 00:45:57.740
It's also what all of those anecdotes
you hear are all about, like

00:45:57.770 --> 00:46:01.480
massaging the scalp or putting
red light on the scalp.

00:46:01.480 --> 00:46:02.680
Although red light might do some other

00:46:02.710 --> 00:46:05.880
things, in general,
heating or lighting of the scalp  or

00:46:05.910 --> 00:46:10.400
massaging of the scalp is really designed
to increase blood flow to the scalp.

00:46:10.430 --> 00:46:15.560
Now, the reason Minoxidil works at all is
because it is going to increase blood

00:46:15.560 --> 00:46:18.120
flow around the clock,
and that's because people are taking it

00:46:18.150 --> 00:46:21.080
topically and it's seeping
into the general circulation,

00:46:21.110 --> 00:46:25.120
or at least it stings somewhat
restricted  to the hair cell niche.

00:46:25.120 --> 00:46:26.600
Or they're taking it orally  and it makes

00:46:26.630 --> 00:46:31.210
it to that hair cell niche
below the follicle.

00:46:31.240 --> 00:46:33.600
When we massage our scalp, however,

00:46:33.630 --> 00:46:36.600
that's a transient thing,
like I massage my scalp right now,

00:46:36.630 --> 00:46:40.040
I'm no doubt
increasing blood flow to certain areas

00:46:40.040 --> 00:46:42.440
and probably decreasing blood flow
to the areas I'm pushing down on.

00:46:42.470 --> 00:46:43.680
But it's all temporary.

00:46:43.710 --> 00:46:48.280
I don't know many people that can massage
their scalp enough during the day or long

00:46:48.310 --> 00:46:52.440
enough during the day  rather that it
would sufficiently increase blood flow.

00:46:52.440 --> 00:46:53.120
With that said,

00:46:53.150 --> 00:46:57.200
it is clear that increasing blood flow
to the scalp by way of reducing

00:46:57.230 --> 00:47:00.080
hypertension,
which is effectively accomplished

00:47:00.110 --> 00:47:05.040
by broadening by expanding the blood
vessels and capillaries,

00:47:05.070 --> 00:47:09.800
is an effective way to at least
hold on to the hair that you have.

00:47:09.830 --> 00:47:12.120
Is it going to completely halt hair loss

00:47:12.120 --> 00:47:14.200
if you have a strong genetic
bias towards hair loss?

00:47:14.230 --> 00:47:16.720
No.
Is it going to reverse hair loss?

00:47:16.750 --> 00:47:18.240
Very unlikely that it will.

00:47:18.270 --> 00:47:22.500
But it can slow hair loss  or even
maintain the hair that you have.

00:47:22.530 --> 00:47:26.760
If we were to take a step back and ask
ourselves what other sorts of drug

00:47:26.790 --> 00:47:30.840
treatments  are out there besides
Minoxidil, that increase blood flow

00:47:30.870 --> 00:47:35.720
and that might increase the rates of hair
growth or more likely  increase

00:47:35.750 --> 00:47:39.940
maintenance of hair that one already has
by increasing blood flow to the niche.

00:47:39.970 --> 00:47:42.080
Nowadays, there are more  and more doctors

00:47:42.110 --> 00:47:45.140
who are familiar with this
requirement for blood flow.

00:47:45.170 --> 00:47:48.400
Understand the mechanisms
by which Minoxidil works and understand

00:47:48.400 --> 00:47:51.160
the vast desire out there for people
to hold on to the hair they have

00:47:51.190 --> 00:47:56.080
and regrow hair and they are prescribing
things like low-dose tadalafil,

00:47:56.110 --> 00:48:00.660
so 2.5 milligram to five
milligram tadalafil.

00:48:00.690 --> 00:48:05.080
Tadalafil was initially discovered
as a drug to treat prostate health.

00:48:05.110 --> 00:48:08.960
It was a drug that we now know  can
increase blood flow to the prostate

00:48:08.990 --> 00:48:13.940
and thereby offset some of the issues
associated with an aging prostate.

00:48:13.970 --> 00:48:16.420
Higher doses of tadalafil

00:48:16.450 --> 00:48:20.200
sometimes also referred to  by its brand
name, which is Cialis,

00:48:20.230 --> 00:48:23.800
are used to treat erectile dysfunction,
but at the dosages that are used

00:48:23.830 --> 00:48:28.240
to increase blood flow to the prostate
and that now a number of doctors are using

00:48:28.270 --> 00:48:31.520
to increase blood flow not just
to the prostate but to all regions

00:48:31.550 --> 00:48:37.940
of the body, including the scalp,
such as 2.5-5 milligram tadalafil.

00:48:37.960 --> 00:48:40.000
This is something that I think  deserves

00:48:40.030 --> 00:48:43.640
attention because it falls under
the umbrella of increasing blood flow

00:48:43.670 --> 00:48:47.660
to the hair stem cell niche
in order to maintain hair.

00:48:47.690 --> 00:48:52.360
It is not something that most doctors
are going to be familiar with as the way

00:48:52.390 --> 00:48:55.360
to reverse hair loss
because it won't do that.

00:48:55.390 --> 00:48:57.240
But the use of low-dose tadalafil

00:48:57.270 --> 00:49:03.140
to slow rates of hair loss is very much
in a logical mechanistic sense,

00:49:03.170 --> 00:49:07.360
exactly the same as the logic of using
Minoxidil to slow rates of hair loss.

00:49:07.390 --> 00:49:09.400
It's all about increasing blood flow

00:49:09.400 --> 00:49:12.080
to support the stem cell niche
below the hair follicle.

00:49:12.110 --> 00:49:16.760
The critical requirement for blood flow,
oxygen and nutrients to the stem cell

00:49:16.790 --> 00:49:21.400
niche is also why you hear a lot nowadays
about the use of PRP,

00:49:21.430 --> 00:49:27.340
platelet-rich plasma for trying to offset
hair loss or even reverse hair loss.

00:49:27.370 --> 00:49:30.020
We're going to do  an entire
episode about PRP.

00:49:30.050 --> 00:49:32.200
It is pretty controversial  in certain

00:49:32.230 --> 00:49:34.780
circles and well- accepted
in other circles.

00:49:34.800 --> 00:49:36.980
A couple of key things
to understand about PRP.

00:49:37.010 --> 00:49:37.840
First of all,

00:49:37.870 --> 00:49:42.860
it is being used  in multiple tissues for
different purposes in different clinics.

00:49:42.890 --> 00:49:44.210
For instance,

00:49:44.240 --> 00:49:46.920
board-certified physicians
in the United States, Canada,

00:49:46.950 --> 00:49:53.800
and Europe are doing PRP injections
into ovaries to try and expand the number

00:49:53.830 --> 00:49:58.320
of healthy follicles and eggs  so
that people can conceive later in life or

00:49:58.320 --> 00:50:00.360
even earlier in life if they
don't have many follicles.

00:50:00.360 --> 00:50:01.880
People are getting PRP injections

00:50:01.910 --> 00:50:05.720
into their joints in order
to try and support joint health.

00:50:05.750 --> 00:50:09.980
People are getting PRP injections  into
just about every tissue you can think of.

00:50:10.010 --> 00:50:15.400
However, PRP, despite what you may
have heard, is not stem cells.

00:50:15.400 --> 00:50:18.560
Somebody tells you they're injecting stem
cells, they're either outside the US,

00:50:18.570 --> 00:50:21.720
Canada, or Northern Europe,
or they're injecting something else.

00:50:21.750 --> 00:50:24.040
So you want to really look into that.

00:50:24.070 --> 00:50:29.960
The safety issues there are subject
totally deserving of an entire episode.

00:50:29.990 --> 00:50:34.320
I'm not necessarily opposed to the future
of stem cells as a treatment,

00:50:34.320 --> 00:50:37.200
but keep in mind that stem cells  are
cells  that can give rise to lots of other

00:50:37.230 --> 00:50:40.900
cell types, and they are cells
that divide and replicate.

00:50:40.920 --> 00:50:42.520
There's a name for that  when it happens

00:50:42.520 --> 00:50:44.460
in the adult body when
you don't want that.

00:50:44.490 --> 00:50:45.760
That's called cancer.

00:50:45.790 --> 00:50:48.480
Tumors are over-production of cells

00:50:48.510 --> 00:50:52.820
from stem cells when those stem cells
ordinarily should be quiescent.

00:50:52.840 --> 00:50:55.080
Keep in mind the difference
between stem cells and PRP.

00:50:55.110 --> 00:50:57.660
PRP, platelet-rich plasma,

00:50:57.690 --> 00:51:02.240
again, is legal in the US and many other
places because it involves  drawing

00:51:02.270 --> 00:51:05.680
somebody's  blood,
spinning it down at a particular speed,

00:51:05.680 --> 00:51:08.560
which separates out different
components within the blood.

00:51:08.590 --> 00:51:10.760
Then taking the platelets  and re-

00:51:10.790 --> 00:51:16.060
injecting those in a solution
back  into the person's body.

00:51:16.090 --> 00:51:21.960
Platelet-rich plasma or PRP is platelet
enriched plasma from that person.

00:51:21.990 --> 00:51:26.200
But the basis of PRP is really
to encourage nutrient delivery

00:51:26.230 --> 00:51:29.840
to a particular region in the body  using
somebody's own platelets,

00:51:29.840 --> 00:51:32.780
because those platelets  are
enriched for various nutrients.

00:51:32.810 --> 00:51:36.560
People are getting PRP
injections  into their scalp.

00:51:36.560 --> 00:51:38.040
Those are not stem cell injections.

00:51:38.070 --> 00:51:42.760
Those are PRP injections into the scalp
with some moderate success.

00:51:42.760 --> 00:51:44.440
These are very expensive treatments.

00:51:44.470 --> 00:51:47.080
They tend to be transiently successful.

00:51:47.080 --> 00:51:49.000
I'm sure there are people out there
who are going to say,

00:51:49.030 --> 00:51:52.280
"PRP worked fabulously well
for me." That might be the case.

00:51:52.280 --> 00:51:53.480
I'm not going to dispute that.

00:51:53.510 --> 00:51:54.640
And I'm happy for you.

00:51:54.670 --> 00:51:56.920
Although there are not sufficient

00:51:56.920 --> 00:51:59.440
clinical data to suggest PRP as
a treatment right now,

00:51:59.440 --> 00:52:02.960
especially given the cost, many thousands
of dollars, many, many treatments.

00:52:02.990 --> 00:52:06.080
It's also the case that the PRP

00:52:06.110 --> 00:52:12.100
injections, when they work, might work
for reasons independent of the platelets.

00:52:12.120 --> 00:52:12.960
What do I mean by that?

00:52:12.960 --> 00:52:15.760
Well, soon, we're going to talk about
a different type of treatment,

00:52:15.790 --> 00:52:19.840
which is a mechanical manipulation
of the hair follicle, typically,

00:52:19.840 --> 00:52:22.080
on the scalp, because that's typically
where people want to regrow hair.

00:52:22.080 --> 00:52:23.280
I don't know many people who are trying

00:52:23.310 --> 00:52:28.040
to maintain or accelerate  or regrow
their back hair, for instance.

00:52:28.040 --> 00:52:28.920
They might be out there,

00:52:28.950 --> 00:52:33.300
but I don't think there are a lot of them
or their leg hair, for that matter.

00:52:33.320 --> 00:52:35.040
Almost always,
it's going to be scalp hair.

00:52:35.070 --> 00:52:39.200
And one way that people are doing
that  is through mechanical stimulation

00:52:39.210 --> 00:52:43.160
of the hair follicle and the stem cell
niche using what's called micro-needling.

00:52:43.190 --> 00:52:45.080
Micro-needling, as the name suggests,

00:52:45.110 --> 00:52:48.860
is taking a bunch of little
needles  either in a little stamp.

00:52:48.890 --> 00:52:52.260
A little square or nowadays,
typically, it's a roller.

00:52:52.280 --> 00:52:53.720
It looks like a paint roller,

00:52:53.750 --> 00:52:58.440
except it's got tons of little
needles  in rows all over that roller.

00:52:58.470 --> 00:53:04.820
Those needles range in length from half
a millimeter to 2.5 millimeters.

00:53:04.850 --> 00:53:08.380
Millimeters and one rolls
that over the scalp.

00:53:08.400 --> 00:53:10.360
If you're thinking, ouch,
that probably hurts.

00:53:10.390 --> 00:53:12.520
Indeed, it can hurt a little bit or a lot,

00:53:12.550 --> 00:53:16.980
depending on the thickness
and the length of those needles.

00:53:17.010 --> 00:53:20.000
Micro-needling has been
shown  to do two things.

00:53:20.030 --> 00:53:23.440
It has been shown  to reactivate semi-

00:53:23.440 --> 00:53:26.720
quiescent populations of stem cells
that are in that telogen phase,

00:53:26.750 --> 00:53:30.480
putting them back in antigen phase
and thereby stimulate more hair growth.

00:53:30.510 --> 00:53:33.880
It has also, and this is I think,
the best use of micro-needling.

00:53:33.910 --> 00:53:36.040
It has also been shown  to be a very

00:53:36.070 --> 00:53:41.800
effective augment for some of the hormone-
based hair regrowth tools

00:53:41.800 --> 00:53:44.940
and pharmacology that we're going
to talk about in a few minutes.

00:53:44.960 --> 00:53:48.040
Micro-needling and PRP  have something
very critical in common,

00:53:48.070 --> 00:53:51.900
which is the needle,
the actual injection into the skin.

00:53:51.920 --> 00:53:53.080
For those of you that are hearing this

00:53:53.110 --> 00:53:56.600
and thinking,
why would disrupting the skin with needles

00:53:56.630 --> 00:54:02.060
actually, support hair growth or regrowth,
wouldn't that just damage the follicle?

00:54:02.090 --> 00:54:07.160
Well, this gets into some of the, I think,
interesting, if not fascinating aspects

00:54:07.190 --> 00:54:10.440
of our biology,
which is that all of the cells in our body

00:54:10.470 --> 00:54:14.780
really can respond to both
chemical and mechanical cues.

00:54:14.810 --> 00:54:19.120
When we hear needle injected into skin,
we think, oh, that must just be damaging

00:54:19.150 --> 00:54:21.520
everything, causing all
sorts of inflammation.

00:54:21.550 --> 00:54:25.520
But it turns out that low levels
of inflammation caused by things like

00:54:25.550 --> 00:54:31.210
micro-needling or PRP injections  or even
the introduction of any kind of fluid.

00:54:31.240 --> 00:54:33.080
For instance, saline fluid injected

00:54:33.110 --> 00:54:37.960
into a region can cause changes
in the cells in that region, causing,

00:54:37.990 --> 00:54:42.760
for instance, stem cell populations
that were waning to reactivate again,

00:54:42.790 --> 00:54:48.760
causing telogen phase follicles that have
melanocytes and stem cells that are dying

00:54:48.790 --> 00:54:53.380
off but not completely gone
to reenter the cell cycle.

00:54:53.410 --> 00:54:58.040
Micro-needling procedures, PRP injections,
things like Minoxidil,

00:54:58.070 --> 00:55:03.000
they all kind of center around  this same
general theme of increasing blood flow,

00:55:03.030 --> 00:55:07.680
increasing oxygen, delivery of nutrients,
or in the case of micro-needling,

00:55:07.710 --> 00:55:13.560
increasing inflammation just enough
at that local site that certain cascades

00:55:13.590 --> 00:55:18.400
of biological function that relate
to proliferation of stem cells or

00:55:18.430 --> 00:55:21.160
maintenance of stem cell
populations  are kicked off.

00:55:21.160 --> 00:55:22.600
It's sort of like reminding the cells

00:55:22.630 --> 00:55:27.040
in that area that they need to stay alive
in order to replenish whatever is lost.

00:55:27.070 --> 00:55:30.360
Sometimes a wound  can
actually induce some healing.

00:55:30.390 --> 00:55:32.480
Although I do want to point out

00:55:32.510 --> 00:55:36.840
that the micro part of micro-needling is
absolutely key  and this should be

00:55:36.870 --> 00:55:39.760
obvious  to you when
you think about scars.

00:55:39.790 --> 00:55:42.800
I don't know about you,
but I've never seen a scar with hair

00:55:42.800 --> 00:55:45.920
growing out of it, or if there was,
it was probably like one hair.

00:55:45.950 --> 00:55:47.980
But if you've ever seen a scar,

00:55:48.000 --> 00:55:50.880
someone had their appendix out  or if
someone had a brain surgery,

00:55:50.910 --> 00:55:54.320
you see that scar because there  is
no hair growing out of it.

00:55:54.350 --> 00:55:58.680
So the micro portion of micro-needling
is extremely important.

00:55:58.710 --> 00:56:00.960
We are not talking about  causing

00:56:00.990 --> 00:56:05.120
significant damage to a tissue in order
to activate  that stem cell population.

00:56:05.150 --> 00:56:07.200
We're talking about causing microdamage

00:56:07.230 --> 00:56:10.600
and micro levels of inflammation
to stimulate growth.

00:56:10.630 --> 00:56:15.040
For those of you that are interested
in using micro-needling or micro-needling

00:56:15.040 --> 00:56:18.040
in combination with chemical treatments
like Minoxidil or some of the other

00:56:18.040 --> 00:56:19.360
treatments we'll talk
about in a little bit.

00:56:19.390 --> 00:56:21.640
Like finasteride and caffeine.

00:56:21.640 --> 00:56:24.520
Yes, believe it or not,
caffeine is being used to regrow hair.

00:56:24.550 --> 00:56:25.680
Very interesting.

00:56:25.680 --> 00:56:26.800
Get into that in a moment.

00:56:26.800 --> 00:56:28.120
But if you're interested in using m

00:56:28.120 --> 00:56:31.580
icro-needling alone or in combination
with some of these other treatments,

00:56:31.600 --> 00:56:34.480
there's a wonderful review that was
just published this last year.

00:56:34.510 --> 00:56:36.900
Wonderful,  because it's
very comprehensive.

00:56:36.930 --> 00:56:38.400
Not so wonderful.

00:56:38.430 --> 00:56:40.940
Not to the fault of the authors  because

00:56:40.970 --> 00:56:44.800
most of the studies out there
on micro-needling are not superb.

00:56:44.830 --> 00:56:48.800
There are ways of gauging the strength
of a study mainly relate to their

00:56:48.800 --> 00:56:51.520
duration,  whether or not they
were control groups et cetera.

00:56:51.520 --> 00:56:54.640
But the review itself  is excellent
and the title of the review is M

00:56:54.670 --> 00:56:58.620
icro-needling and its Use in
Hair Loss Disorders: A Systematic Review.

00:56:58.640 --> 00:56:59.800
We will provide a link to this

00:56:59.830 --> 00:57:04.320
in the show note captions and this review
did a very good job of highlighting both

00:57:04.320 --> 00:57:07.880
the strengths and drawbacks of the various
studies looking at micro-needling.

00:57:07.910 --> 00:57:10.280
It also explored the use of micro-needling

00:57:10.310 --> 00:57:15.640
in both men and women and of various
ages,  and it does appear to be the case

00:57:15.670 --> 00:57:19.240
that micro-needling shows some positive
benefit in both men and women,

00:57:19.270 --> 00:57:22.840
regardless of age,
especially when used in combination

00:57:22.840 --> 00:57:25.080
with the various other treatments
that we're talking about.

00:57:25.080 --> 00:57:29.200
I was also able to glean from this review
and some of the papers described within it

00:57:29.230 --> 00:57:34.040
that needle lengths  of about one
millimeter  to 2.5 millimeters seem to be

00:57:34.070 --> 00:57:37.360
more effective  than
shorter needle lengths.

00:57:37.390 --> 00:57:40.480
So if you're scared of the needles
and the needle lengths,

00:57:40.510 --> 00:57:44.480
keep in mind that done properly,
micro-needling shouldn't be too painful.

00:57:44.480 --> 00:57:46.040
Some people experience  a little bit more

00:57:46.040 --> 00:57:49.120
pain than others, but it's not
considered  a very painful procedure.

00:57:49.150 --> 00:57:51.920
It is, however, a procedure that can cause

00:57:51.920 --> 00:57:54.880
some bleeding of the scalp,
and that bleeding of the scalp can be

00:57:54.880 --> 00:57:57.000
very apparent,
especially if it's in the front

00:57:57.000 --> 00:58:00.520
of the head as opposed to in the top
of the head and hidden by some hair or if

00:58:00.550 --> 00:58:04.700
you're already
quite bald in a given region.

00:58:04.730 --> 00:58:05.840
Keep that in mind.

00:58:05.840 --> 00:58:07.480
I suppose one could wear a hat  or a wig

00:58:07.480 --> 00:58:09.800
or something of that sort if they
were  really self-conscious  about it.

00:58:09.830 --> 00:58:13.080
But the micro-needling itself is causing

00:58:13.110 --> 00:58:17.200
a physical disruption to the scalp,
some degree of bleeding, inflammation.

00:58:17.230 --> 00:58:19.080
And again, all of that is part

00:58:19.110 --> 00:58:23.020
of the process by which micro-needling
can actually improve hair growth.

00:58:23.040 --> 00:58:24.760
Of course, there's healing that occurs

00:58:24.760 --> 00:58:26.800
of the bleeding  and the
damage to the follicle.

00:58:26.830 --> 00:58:28.240
This is a transient thing,

00:58:28.260 --> 00:58:31.960
but understanding the cosmetic
implications in the short term as well as

00:58:31.960 --> 00:58:34.200
in the long-term  is
certainly worth knowing.

00:58:34.200 --> 00:58:35.440
One thing that's very clear  is

00:58:35.470 --> 00:58:39.720
that the combination of micro-needling
and Minoxidil treatment together  is far

00:58:39.750 --> 00:58:42.360
more effective than either
of those treatments alone.

00:58:42.390 --> 00:58:43.480
In addition,

00:58:43.510 --> 00:58:47.320
the combination of micro-needling
and Minoxidil has been shown to be

00:58:47.320 --> 00:58:49.820
effective in recovering
what are called dead zones.

00:58:49.850 --> 00:58:53.880
These are regions of the scalp that are
either completely bald or mostly bald,

00:58:53.910 --> 00:58:59.180
for which there is essentially
no stem cell population there.

00:58:59.210 --> 00:59:01.480
The combination of Minoxidil  plus

00:59:01.480 --> 00:59:05.320
micro-needling is somehow able to recover
those stem cell populations  and allow

00:59:05.350 --> 00:59:08.040
new hair to grow,
although the growth of that hair

00:59:08.070 --> 00:59:13.040
in those dead zone regions can take
a very long  time,  30 to even 50 weeks.

00:59:13.070 --> 00:59:15.240
Neither Minoxidil treatment alone  nor

00:59:15.240 --> 00:59:19.280
micro-needling alone has been shown to be
effective in recovering  these so-called

00:59:19.310 --> 00:59:22.660
dead zones when those
treatments are done separately.

00:59:22.680 --> 00:59:23.400
This, I would say,

00:59:23.430 --> 00:59:28.240
is a strong reason to consider combining
micro-needling  and Minoxidil as opposed

00:59:28.270 --> 00:59:30.980
to just doing Minoxidil
or just micro-needling.

00:59:31.010 --> 00:59:35.160
I should also mention  that Minoxidil
treatment, if you pursue it,

00:59:35.160 --> 00:59:38.920
is likely something that you are going
to have to do for the rest of your life.

00:59:38.950 --> 00:59:43.880
If you want to hold on to the hair growth
that you obtain with Minoxidil or if you

00:59:43.910 --> 00:59:48.240
want to maintain the hair that you are
already maintaining with Minoxidil.

00:59:48.270 --> 00:59:52.600
Some people have been successful
in taking Minoxidil, maintaining some hair

00:59:52.600 --> 00:59:55.760
growth  or even stimulating some hair
growth and then coming off Minoxidil.

00:59:55.790 --> 00:59:57.960
But most everyone who goes on Minoxidil

00:59:57.990 --> 01:00:01.560
has to stay on Minoxidil because when
they  cease taking Minoxidil,

01:00:01.590 --> 01:00:05.760
even if they're doing other treatments,
they lose the hair  that they gained

01:00:05.790 --> 01:00:08.600
with Minoxidil, so that is
an important consideration.

01:00:08.600 --> 01:00:10.600
The decision to go on Minoxidil is likely

01:00:10.630 --> 01:00:13.460
a decision to be on Minoxidil
for the rest of your life.

