01:01:26.000 --> 01:01:28.840
So, as you're probably starting
to realize, there's a relationship between

01:01:28.870 --> 01:01:33.120
mechanical stimulation of the follicle
and blood flow, both of which turn out

01:01:33.150 --> 01:01:37.460
to be  critical  for maintaining hair
and for stimulating hair growth.

01:01:37.490 --> 01:01:42.920
Not surprisingly then, an increasingly c
ommon treatment  for hair loss is Botox.

01:01:42.950 --> 01:01:48.520
Botox is the brand name for what is
otherwise known as botulinum neurotoxin.

01:01:48.550 --> 01:01:50.740
What is botulinum neurotoxin?

01:01:50.770 --> 01:01:52.040
Botulinum neurotoxin,

01:01:52.070 --> 01:01:56.280
sometimes just called botulinum
for short, is a toxin that's a bacterial

01:01:56.310 --> 01:02:02.600
toxin that serves  to cut the protein
that leads  to synaptic vesicle release.

01:02:02.630 --> 01:02:04.320
What in the world did I just say?

01:02:04.320 --> 01:02:07.120
Well, when your nerve cells communicate
with one another,

01:02:07.150 --> 01:02:11.360
they do that by way of electricity,
but the electricity within those nerve

01:02:11.390 --> 01:02:14.320
cells,  those neurons,
triggers the release of chemicals

01:02:14.350 --> 01:02:18.060
from neurons into the synapse,
the little gap between neurons.

01:02:18.090 --> 01:02:22.040
The release of those chemicals allows
the next neuron to be chemically active,

01:02:22.070 --> 01:02:26.700
or in some cases, it will suppress the
electrical activity of that next neuron.

01:02:26.730 --> 01:02:32.880
Botulinum neurotoxin serves  to cut
a protein present in neurons so

01:02:32.910 --> 01:02:37.900
that neurons  cannot release the chemicals
that cause other neurons to be active.

01:02:37.930 --> 01:02:39.600
This actually is pretty serious.

01:02:39.600 --> 01:02:41.520
If you were to get botulinum neurotoxin

01:02:41.550 --> 01:02:46.000
injected into your muscle you would be
paralyzed because the nerves that control

01:02:46.030 --> 01:02:49.480
contraction of the muscles would not be
able to control the release

01:02:49.510 --> 01:02:53.420
of that chemical onto the muscle,
which makes it contract.

01:02:53.450 --> 01:02:57.720
Botulinum neurotoxin  is commonly
used in what's called Botox.

01:02:57.720 --> 01:02:59.360
Botox is something  most people are

01:02:59.390 --> 01:03:04.280
familiar with because people get it
injected  in and around their wrinkles

01:03:04.310 --> 01:03:10.040
because many wrinkles are triggered
by not  just loss of tensile strength

01:03:10.070 --> 01:03:14.360
in the skin, but rather,
the nerves around the skin

01:03:14.390 --> 01:03:18.460
and in the skin are hyper contracted,
which causes wrinkles.

01:03:18.480 --> 01:03:19.840
For instance, I have crow's feet.

01:03:19.840 --> 01:03:22.640
I like to think that's because I've
laughed a lot and smiled a lot,

01:03:22.640 --> 01:03:25.700
and it's probably also because
I've squinted a lot in my lifetime.

01:03:25.730 --> 01:03:27.800
I have crow's feet  because the nerves

01:03:27.830 --> 01:03:33.160
there have pinched the skin  on either
side  of my eyes and that's given me

01:03:33.160 --> 01:03:36.200
little creases there that are
sometimes referred to  as crow's feet.

01:03:36.230 --> 01:03:37.920
Botox injections  can be applied

01:03:37.950 --> 01:03:42.900
to the scalp in order
to relieve tension of the scalp.

01:03:42.920 --> 01:03:44.560
In hearing that,  it should be obvious why

01:03:44.590 --> 01:03:47.720
Botox is being used to try
and offset hair loss.

01:03:47.750 --> 01:03:50.600
It's decreasing the squinting,

01:03:50.630 --> 01:03:57.160
if you will, or the tensile nature
of the scalp skin so that more blood flow

01:03:57.190 --> 01:04:00.380
can arrive at that stem
cell follicle area.

01:04:00.410 --> 01:04:03.840
Botox treatment to the scalp is
actually becoming pretty common.

01:04:03.840 --> 01:04:06.280
There are a couple requirements
with this Botox treatment.

01:04:06.280 --> 01:04:08.920
First of all, it has to be done
by somebody who's really skilled.

01:04:08.950 --> 01:04:11.840
There are numerous images online

01:04:11.870 --> 01:04:16.400
and websites online of so-called Botox
fails, where people have gotten too much

01:04:16.430 --> 01:04:20.800
Botox or the injections  have been done
too deep or not at the correct locations

01:04:20.800 --> 01:04:24.320
on people's face or scalp, and it can
give them  droopy  scalp or droopy eyes.

01:04:24.350 --> 01:04:27.920
All sorts of cosmetic nightmares
can occur with Botox.

01:04:27.940 --> 01:04:31.440
The second thing to understand is
that Botox does eventually wear off.

01:04:31.470 --> 01:04:34.860
That botulinum neurotoxin
doesn't stick around forever.

01:04:34.880 --> 01:04:37.000
Provided it's done correctly
at the correct dosages,

01:04:37.030 --> 01:04:40.700
it doesn't actually kill the neurons
that cause that tension of the skin,

01:04:40.730 --> 01:04:43.820
so Botox injections have
to be done repeatedly.

01:04:43.850 --> 01:04:48.040
The efficacy of Botox for offsetting
hair loss is not clear.

01:04:48.040 --> 01:04:51.080
There aren't a lot of large- scale
clinical studies on this just yet,

01:04:51.110 --> 01:04:54.760
but it does seem to be at least one
reasonably safe alternative to things

01:04:54.790 --> 01:04:59.040
like  Minoxidil, although I think if one
were to just want to increase blood flow

01:04:59.070 --> 01:05:03.080
to the scalp, things like low- dose
Tadalafil, which doesn't seem to carry any

01:05:03.080 --> 01:05:06.920
of the side effects that Minoxidil can
carry, we talked about  those side effects

01:05:06.950 --> 01:05:09.680
earlier, that would probably
be the better alternative.

01:05:09.710 --> 01:05:14.000
Botox is a fairly invasive procedure,
but some people opt for Botox treatment.

01:05:14.030 --> 01:05:19.400
In fact, there is a syndrome called
cutis verticis gyrata.

01:05:19.400 --> 01:05:20.760
Some of you have probably seen this.

01:05:20.760 --> 01:05:23.480
It's more typical in men,
although it does occur in women.

01:05:23.510 --> 01:05:29.700
It literally means a lumping of the skin
on the scalp, or gyri of the scalp.

01:05:29.730 --> 01:05:36.300
Gyri or gyrus  pertains to the Latin
word knee, so it means bump or knee.

01:05:36.330 --> 01:05:38.140
Any time you hear the word gyrus

01:05:38.170 --> 01:05:41.340
in neuroscience or in biology,
you're talking about a bump.

01:05:41.360 --> 01:05:44.000
You'll sometimes see people will have
ridges in the back where it looks as if

01:05:44.030 --> 01:05:48.840
the skin was pushed together, kind
of like a Shar-Pei dog, but on the scalp.

01:05:48.870 --> 01:05:54.920
People with cutis  verticis gyrata almost
always experience pattern hair loss.

01:05:54.920 --> 01:05:56.480
Now, part of the reason for that is

01:05:56.510 --> 01:06:01.400
cutis verticis gyrata
is also associated with some androgen  or

01:06:01.400 --> 01:06:04.880
testosterone- related hormone issues
that we'll talk about in a little bit.

01:06:04.910 --> 01:06:06.760
But in addition to that,

01:06:06.790 --> 01:06:10.920
it has been shown that  relieving some
of those gyrata by injections of Botox

01:06:10.950 --> 01:06:14.720
to allow those folds to sit flatter,
A, is effective.

01:06:14.750 --> 01:06:20.320
It can lead to less of those gyri,
those bumps, and can improve hair growth

01:06:20.350 --> 01:06:24.040
in those regions,
even if those people don't  take on any

01:06:24.070 --> 01:06:26.940
additional treatments
to address the hormone issues.

01:06:26.960 --> 01:06:30.200
That's really how people arrived at this
understanding that Botox might be  a good

01:06:30.230 --> 01:06:35.720
treatment in general for reducing the
squinting of the scalp  that can occur

01:06:35.750 --> 01:06:38.040
and the resulting  hair
loss in those regions.

01:06:38.070 --> 01:06:42.160
I'd now like to turn our attention
to the chemical variables that control

01:06:42.190 --> 01:06:46.600
the duration  of the growth phase of hair,
the duration of that catagen phase,

01:06:46.630 --> 01:06:50.680
which is when that hair essentially
recedes from the inside out,

01:06:50.710 --> 01:06:55.820
and the quiescent or semi-
quiescent telogen phase.

01:06:55.850 --> 01:07:00.340
There are a couple of key chemical players
here that we should all be aware of.

01:07:00.370 --> 01:07:04.460
First of all, the growth factor IGF-1,

01:07:04.490 --> 01:07:07.520
insulin growth factor 1,
which is produced by the liver,

01:07:07.550 --> 01:07:11.760
but that receives stimulation
from the brain and pituitary to be

01:07:11.790 --> 01:07:15.540
released, is a strong
regulator of hair growth.

01:07:15.570 --> 01:07:19.460
We can think of it  as
the accelerator on hair growth.

01:07:19.490 --> 01:07:24.960
It does that by extending  that anagen,
or growth phase, for longer.

01:07:24.990 --> 01:07:27.120
It doesn't necessarily speed up growth,

01:07:27.150 --> 01:07:30.260
but it extends it  for
a longer period of time.

01:07:30.290 --> 01:07:33.880
In addition, cyclic AMP,
which is part of what's called a second

01:07:33.910 --> 01:07:37.680
messenger pathway, in fact,
cyclic AMP is a second messenger,

01:07:37.710 --> 01:07:41.760
is also a key player in stimulating
growth of the hair follicle.

01:07:41.760 --> 01:07:45.520
Now, cyclic AMP does many different things
in many different cell types in the body.

01:07:45.550 --> 01:07:47.960
It really acts, as the name suggests,

01:07:47.990 --> 01:07:52.280
as a messenger between signals
that arrive at the surface of cells

01:07:52.310 --> 01:07:57.240
and transmitting  or conveying those
signals to things that happen  deep within

01:07:57.270 --> 01:08:01.210
the cells, such as the turning
on and off  of various genes.

01:08:01.240 --> 01:08:04.560
When you hear second messenger, don't
let that confuse you  or overwhelm you.

01:08:04.590 --> 01:08:08.520
Just understand that the whole process
of getting signals  from the outside

01:08:08.550 --> 01:08:12.760
of cells into the center of cells
and controlling gene expression,

01:08:12.790 --> 01:08:16.760
for instance,
causing a stem cell to continue to give

01:08:16.790 --> 01:08:20.740
off daughter cells, or causing a hair cell
to continue growing for longer,

01:08:20.760 --> 01:08:24.600
that whole process  is a bit like
a bucket brigade of handing off water or

01:08:24.630 --> 01:08:27.840
a bucket from one component
to the next, or along a chain.

01:08:27.840 --> 01:08:28.920
It's like an assembly line.

01:08:28.920 --> 01:08:31.380
I think that's probably
the simplest way to think about it.

01:08:31.410 --> 01:08:35.840
For sake of this discussion,
IGF-1 is known to increase the growth

01:08:35.870 --> 01:08:41.020
of hair by extending that anagen phase,
as is cyclic AMP.

01:08:41.040 --> 01:08:42.440
Those are going to be considered

01:08:42.460 --> 01:08:45.500
the accelerators,
at least in this conversation.

01:08:45.530 --> 01:08:49.320
The brakes on hair growth are going to be

01:08:49.340 --> 01:08:52.960
the things  that either shorten
the anagen  phase or that extend

01:08:52.990 --> 01:08:58.020
the catagen phase or this quiescent phase,
which is the telogen phase.

01:08:58.050 --> 01:09:00.520
The two major brakes on hair growth

01:09:00.550 --> 01:09:05.540
that we want to think about are PDE,
which is a phosphodiesterase,

01:09:05.570 --> 01:09:10.700
anytime you hear -ase it's likely
to be an enzyme, and TGF-beta-2.

01:09:10.720 --> 01:09:13.500
This is a particular growth factor that,

01:09:13.520 --> 01:09:15.960
somewhat counterintuitively,
doesn't stimulate growth,

01:09:15.990 --> 01:09:19.100
it actually stimulates lack of growth,
or shortens growth.

01:09:19.130 --> 01:09:23.200
With all of that in mind,
and please do also keep in mind that you

01:09:23.200 --> 01:09:25.880
don't need to remember all those specific
terms, just understand that there are

01:09:25.910 --> 01:09:30.560
some factors, like insulin growth factor
1, that act as accelerators  on growth,

01:09:30.590 --> 01:09:33.620
and there are factors
that act as brakes on growth.

01:09:33.640 --> 01:09:35.880
We can start to think about why,

01:09:35.910 --> 01:09:41.320
for instance, half of all people
by age 50  start to lose their hair.

01:09:41.320 --> 01:09:44.560
Well, they start to lose their hair
because of something called androgen-

01:09:44.590 --> 01:09:48.280
related alopecia, which,
translated to English,

01:09:48.300 --> 01:09:53.720
means testosterone and  testosterone-
derivative induced hair loss.

01:09:53.750 --> 01:09:55.780
This is true in men and women.

01:09:55.800 --> 01:09:59.700
Hearing that, you should probably  be
wondering the following thing:

01:09:59.720 --> 01:10:04.380
Young men have higher levels
of testosterone than old men, right?

01:10:04.400 --> 01:10:05.600
Well, the answer is yes,

01:10:05.630 --> 01:10:10.200
although some older men in their 40s,
50s, even 80s, maintain testosterone

01:10:10.220 --> 01:10:13.560
levels similar to many men
in their 20s, but most don't.

01:10:13.590 --> 01:10:16.960
It's a downward slope
starting at about age 40.

01:10:16.990 --> 01:10:20.300
How steep that downward slope is depends.

01:10:20.330 --> 01:10:22.240
Women, too, have testosterone.

01:10:22.260 --> 01:10:26.900
In fact, women have higher levels
of testosterone than they do estrogen.

01:10:26.920 --> 01:10:28.220
That's right.

01:10:28.250 --> 01:10:32.000
A healthy woman has higher levels
of testosterone than she does estrogen.

01:10:32.030 --> 01:10:34.120
However, women, on average,

01:10:34.140 --> 01:10:39.280
have lower testosterone than most men,
so they still have far more estrogen

01:10:39.300 --> 01:10:43.560
and far less testosterone than most men,
but the level of testosterone that they

01:10:43.590 --> 01:10:48.540
have within their body is higher than
the level  of estrogen they have.

01:10:48.570 --> 01:10:52.120
Androgens such as  testosterone  and its

01:10:52.140 --> 01:10:57.320
derivatives, such as dihydrotestosterone,
which will be much the topic of what we're

01:10:57.340 --> 01:11:03.960
getting into next,
inhibit IGF-1 and cyclic AMP.

01:11:04.320 --> 01:11:08.080
Again, androgens such as
dihydrotestosterone inhibit,

01:11:08.110 --> 01:11:13.120
prevent the action of IGF-1 and cyclic
AMP, which you just learned a few moments

01:11:13.140 --> 01:11:16.200
ago, act to extend the anagen
or growth phase of hair.

01:11:16.220 --> 01:11:21.400
Which then raises the question, well,
if young people, both male and female,

01:11:21.420 --> 01:11:24.920
have higher levels of testosterone than
they do when they're older,

01:11:24.950 --> 01:11:29.340
why would people lose their hair
when they're older and not younger?

01:11:29.370 --> 01:11:34.600
The answer lies  in the conversion
of testosterone  to dihydrotestosterone.

01:11:34.630 --> 01:11:36.680
Testosterone most people have heard of.

01:11:36.710 --> 01:11:41.520
Dihydrotestosterone, or DHT,
is made from testosterone.

01:11:41.550 --> 01:11:45.440
There's an enzyme  called  5-alpha
reductase that converts testosterone

01:11:45.460 --> 01:11:48.900
into  dihydrotestosterone
in both men and women.

01:11:48.920 --> 01:11:53.800
Dihydrotestosterone  binds
to the androgen receptor at five times

01:11:53.830 --> 01:11:57.760
the affinity of testosterone,
so it is the most powerful androgen

01:11:57.790 --> 01:12:01.720
in humans, and it is responsible
for a number of  things that we  all

01:12:01.750 --> 01:12:08.040
really want and like, such as
mental vigor,  physical vigor, strength,

01:12:08.070 --> 01:12:12.580
healing capacity, drive,
libido, and on and on.

01:12:12.610 --> 01:12:14.700
DHT itself is not bad.

01:12:14.720 --> 01:12:17.760
If we take a step back  and we
acknowledge testosterone levels are

01:12:17.790 --> 01:12:21.040
higher  in males and females at younger
ages as opposed to older,

01:12:21.070 --> 01:12:24.840
but as they get older,
there is more 5-alpha reductase  activity,

01:12:24.840 --> 01:12:26.920
which is converting more
of that  testosterone

01:12:26.950 --> 01:12:30.400
to dihydrotestosterone
and dihydrotestosterone inhibits hair

01:12:30.420 --> 01:12:35.160
growth by reducing IGF-1 and cyclic AMP,
well, then we should all be aboard why it

01:12:35.180 --> 01:12:40.600
is that by age 50, about 50% of people
experience pattern hair loss.

01:12:40.630 --> 01:12:43.940
That is androgen-dependent alopecia,

01:12:43.960 --> 01:12:48.140
but translated to normal
English is pattern hair loss.

01:12:48.170 --> 01:12:52.280
In a moment you'll understand  why some
people lose their hair from the crown

01:12:52.300 --> 01:12:55.280
region in the back of the head,
or back and top of the head,

01:12:55.300 --> 01:12:59.160
whereas other people lose their hair
in the front of their head,

01:12:59.180 --> 01:13:02.840
in the flanks,
right on either side of the midline,

01:13:02.870 --> 01:13:06.220
or maybe in the midline
and front altogether.

01:13:06.250 --> 01:13:10.080
That's because different people,
depending on their genetic lineage,

01:13:10.110 --> 01:13:13.980
have different patterns of androgen
receptors on their scalp.

01:13:14.000 --> 01:13:15.720
The pattern of androgen receptors

01:13:15.750 --> 01:13:19.940
that you inherit indeed does
come from your mother's side.

01:13:19.960 --> 01:13:23.560
This is what gave rise to the the myth
that if you want to know  if you're going

01:13:23.590 --> 01:13:26.260
to go bald or not, just look
at your mother's father.

01:13:26.280 --> 01:13:27.440
Doesn't quite work that way.

01:13:27.460 --> 01:13:31.480
In fact, if you think about the logic,
you should really look at your mother's

01:13:31.500 --> 01:13:36.800
mother if you want to know your pattern
of androgen receptors on your scalp.

01:13:36.830 --> 01:13:38.960
However, most women  don't lose as much

01:13:38.990 --> 01:13:42.320
hair from their scalp,
or they have ways of covering up the hair

01:13:42.320 --> 01:13:45.640
loss in their scalp because their hair is
just generally  longer or they're using

01:13:45.670 --> 01:13:50.080
other approaches, so that you never really
get a clear picture of what the androgen-

01:13:50.110 --> 01:13:53.860
dependent hair loss was
in your grandmother.

01:13:53.880 --> 01:13:56.960
Now, we don't want to go too far down
the genetics rabbit hole because,

01:13:56.960 --> 01:14:00.480
as you know,  you can't select your
parents anyway, but if you want to know

01:14:00.500 --> 01:14:03.960
why, for instance,
I'm losing a bit of hair on  either side

01:14:03.990 --> 01:14:07.560
of the midline in the front,
it almost certainly  has to do

01:14:07.560 --> 01:14:10.800
with the fact that I have a higher density
of androgen receptors there,

01:14:10.800 --> 01:14:13.160
as opposed to, say,
on the crown of my head  where,

01:14:13.160 --> 01:14:15.520
for whatever reason,
my hair seems to grow thickest.

01:14:15.550 --> 01:14:17.420
Other people lose hair on the crown,

01:14:17.450 --> 01:14:22.060
in the back and top, but not in the front,
and some people will lose it all over.

01:14:22.090 --> 01:14:26.420
Now you understand why hair loss
occurs in certain regions of the body.

01:14:26.450 --> 01:14:30.720
You should also understand
that the androgen receptors on the face

01:14:30.750 --> 01:14:33.340
are also what are responsible
for beard growth.

01:14:33.360 --> 01:14:36.040
This is where  it can get  a little bit
tricky, but a lot of things  will start

01:14:36.070 --> 01:14:39.260
to make sense if you can understand
this and internalize this.

01:14:39.290 --> 01:14:41.360
If you have a high density  of androgen

01:14:41.380 --> 01:14:45.000
receptors on your face,
well then as your DHT levels  go up

01:14:45.030 --> 01:14:48.360
with age, you will be able to grow
a thicker and thicker beard.

01:14:48.380 --> 01:14:51.040
In fact, it is rare to see someone who can

01:14:51.070 --> 01:14:54.520
grow a thick beard in their youth,
but not so much as they get older.

01:14:54.550 --> 01:14:56.460
In fact, the reverse tends to be true.

01:14:56.480 --> 01:14:58.160
The pattern of androgen receptors differs

01:14:58.180 --> 01:15:02.180
between the scalp
and the face and the back.

01:15:02.210 --> 01:15:06.460
On your back you have androgen  receptors
and their DHT  stimulates hair growth.

01:15:06.480 --> 01:15:09.520
If you know someone who has a very hairy
back, or if you have a very hairy  back,

01:15:09.520 --> 01:15:12.360
that means you have a high density
of androgen receptors on your back.

01:15:12.380 --> 01:15:14.560
If you have a beard and that beard is

01:15:14.560 --> 01:15:17.920
thick, well then you have a high density
of androgen receptors on your face.

01:15:17.950 --> 01:15:22.080
However, a high density of androgen
receptors anywhere on your scalp is going

01:15:22.110 --> 01:15:27.240
to predispose those regions to androgen-
dependent alopecia, or hair loss in those

01:15:27.260 --> 01:15:30.640
particular regions,
which is going to allow us to understand

01:15:30.670 --> 01:15:34.720
why all of the rest of the treatments
for halting hair loss

01:15:34.750 --> 01:15:40.600
and for stimulating hair growth,
almost all of those center on inhibiting

01:15:40.630 --> 01:15:46.900
either DHT directly, or 5-alpha reductase,
the conversion  of testosterone to DHT.

01:15:46.920 --> 01:15:50.760
Now I'd like to discuss the ways that one
can chemically adjust certain things

01:15:50.790 --> 01:15:57.340
within  the hair growth pathway,
things like IGF-1, PDE, TGF beta, etc,

01:15:57.370 --> 01:16:00.520
in order to stimulate hair
growth  or halt hair loss.

01:16:00.520 --> 01:16:02.120
The first thing on this list is actually

01:16:02.140 --> 01:16:06.020
going to be pretty surprising to a number
of you,  and that's caffeine.

01:16:06.040 --> 01:16:08.680
We all think of caffeine  as
a stimulant that we drink.

01:16:08.710 --> 01:16:10.860
I certainly drink coffee in Yerba Mate,

01:16:10.880 --> 01:16:12.880
the occasional energy drink,
things of that sort.

01:16:12.910 --> 01:16:15.000
Caffeine does many things besides

01:16:15.000 --> 01:16:18.620
stimulate our central nervous system
and make us feel less sleepy, however.

01:16:18.640 --> 01:16:25.380
One of the things that caffeine  does  is
it is a fairly  potent PDE inhibitor.

01:16:25.410 --> 01:16:30.620
By being a potent PDE inhibitor,
it indirectly stimulates IGF-1.

01:16:30.640 --> 01:16:31.160
Why?

01:16:31.180 --> 01:16:38.060
Well, because PDE can suppress IGF-1,
and by ingesting caffeine,

01:16:38.090 --> 01:16:43.820
or by applying topical caffeine ointment
or cream  to the scalp,

01:16:43.840 --> 01:16:49.120
you can suppress PDE sufficiently enough
to increase IGF-1 and increase some hair

01:16:49.140 --> 01:16:52.860
growth, or at least maintain
hair growth in that region.

01:16:52.880 --> 01:16:54.320
This may come as a shock,

01:16:54.340 --> 01:16:58.520
it might seem a little bit esoteric
or even  outside the margins  of typical

01:16:58.550 --> 01:17:02.960
treatments, but head to head,
topical caffeine application can be as

01:17:02.990 --> 01:17:07.280
effective  as Minoxidil application
without actually  lowering things  like

01:17:07.300 --> 01:17:12.860
blood pressure and potentially increasing
prolactin and some of the other negative,

01:17:12.880 --> 01:17:16.820
let's call them negative  because
they are,  side effects of Minoxidil.

01:17:16.840 --> 01:17:21.040
Caffeine ointments, and caffeine present
in various hair treatments

01:17:21.070 --> 01:17:25.620
and creams, etc, is starting to become
a more  prominent theme out there.

01:17:25.640 --> 01:17:30.240
I will include a reference to caffeine
and its uses for offsetting hair loss.

01:17:30.240 --> 01:17:33.760
Keep in mind that  topical caffeine
ointments shouldn't necessarily be applied

01:17:33.760 --> 01:17:37.160
every single day, so this is the sort of
thing  you might do three times a week.

01:17:37.160 --> 01:17:40.400
The concentration of caffeine in
different ointments varies tremendously.

01:17:40.420 --> 01:17:42.320
Most of the studies  of caffeine

01:17:42.320 --> 01:17:46.440
on the stem cell niches that control hair
growth and extension of the anagen phase

01:17:46.460 --> 01:17:49.360
of hair growth have been
performed in vitro in a dish.

01:17:49.380 --> 01:17:54.000
Although there are some  clinical studies
exploring this, they are not nearly as

01:17:54.000 --> 01:17:57.520
extensive in number or duration as
the studies of Minoxidil because this

01:17:57.520 --> 01:17:59.600
approach  just hasn't
been around quite as long.

01:17:59.630 --> 01:18:03.640
However, when comparing  side effects
of Minoxidil, cost of Minoxidil,

01:18:03.670 --> 01:18:06.200
comparing the efficacy of caffeine
and Minoxidil,

01:18:06.220 --> 01:18:10.600
I think caffeine as a topical treatment
for offsetting hair loss stands as

01:18:10.630 --> 01:18:14.140
a pretty good choice if you're  going
to start exploring this pathway.

01:18:14.160 --> 01:18:17.240
There's no reason to think that if you
were to try the caffeine ointment and it

01:18:17.240 --> 01:18:20.200
didn't work for you  or you didn't like
it for some reason or you needed to stop

01:18:20.200 --> 01:18:22.440
it  for some reason,
that you couldn't stop it  safely,

01:18:22.460 --> 01:18:26.280
because it doesn't carry all the other
blood pressure- related effects

01:18:26.300 --> 01:18:29.460
and prolactin emia effects
that Minoxidil does.

01:18:29.480 --> 01:18:32.960
If you look out there  into the hair
maintenance and hair replacement

01:18:32.960 --> 01:18:35.280
literature,
and you  look at thetreatments that are

01:18:35.300 --> 01:18:38.100
being sold, don't be surprised
to see caffeine there.

01:18:38.120 --> 01:18:40.080
Also, don't be surprised when I tell you

01:18:40.080 --> 01:18:43.520
what I'm about to tell you now, which is,
no, you can't simply  just drink  more

01:18:43.550 --> 01:18:47.480
caffeine in order to accomplish
the goal of offsetting hair loss.

01:18:47.480 --> 01:18:50.360
It is true that when you ingest
caffeine, it goes systemically.

01:18:50.380 --> 01:18:54.120
However, you have so many adenosine
receptors throughout your body.

01:18:54.120 --> 01:18:57.200
Those adenosine receptors,
and the parking of caffeine in those

01:18:57.200 --> 01:18:59.680
adenosine receptors,
is the main way  in which  caffeine

01:18:59.710 --> 01:19:03.940
exerts its stimulatory effects,
making you feel less sleepy.

01:19:03.960 --> 01:19:06.040
It does that because then  adenosine can't

01:19:06.040 --> 01:19:08.200
have its effects,
which are to make you sleepy.

01:19:08.220 --> 01:19:11.100
Well, those adenosine receptors soak up

01:19:11.130 --> 01:19:14.720
so much of the caffeine  that you would
ingest orally that very,

01:19:14.750 --> 01:19:19.160
very little would make it  to the scalp
and to the hair follicles

01:19:19.160 --> 01:19:22.080
at the concentrations that you would want,
so that's why you have to rely

01:19:22.110 --> 01:19:25.940
on the  application of these caffeine
ointments about three times a week.

01:19:25.960 --> 01:19:27.680
Keep in mind that  no one has really

01:19:27.710 --> 01:19:31.400
explored the dosages of caffeine
in these ointments in a systematic way.

01:19:31.400 --> 01:19:34.720
We are still in  the early stages of all
this, but I do think it's important

01:19:34.730 --> 01:19:38.080
to mention caffeine because of the lower
incidence of side effects,

01:19:38.080 --> 01:19:40.880
at least reported side effects,
and the general safety margins,

01:19:40.910 --> 01:19:44.600
and the head to head essentially
comparable efficacy  with Minoxidil

01:19:44.600 --> 01:19:46.840
because  Minoxidil has
a bunch of other issues.

01:19:46.870 --> 01:19:51.080
Now keep in mind that  both Minoxidil
and caffeine are generally used as

01:19:51.110 --> 01:19:55.200
a preventative for reducing
hair loss over time.

01:19:55.220 --> 01:19:58.720
They are not expected,
and they do not, as far- as far as we

01:19:58.750 --> 01:20:03.120
know, create new hair growth
to any sufficient degree.

01:20:03.120 --> 01:20:06.680
If any of you have used caffeine,
ointments or minoxidil and observed  new

01:20:06.680 --> 01:20:09.840
hair growth that was robust,
please put that in the comment section.

01:20:09.840 --> 01:20:12.600
I'd be curious about those experiences,
but as far as I know

01:20:12.600 --> 01:20:16.320
and from  the clinical  literature that I
read, there's no examples of that.

01:20:16.340 --> 01:20:18.000
One other point about caffeine.

01:20:18.030 --> 01:20:22.960
It does appear that caffeine can not only
indirectly stimulate IGF-1 and the antigen

01:20:22.990 --> 01:20:27.200
phase of hair cell growth by way
of reducing PD and TGF beta.

01:20:27.220 --> 01:20:30.200
But it also seems to reduce apoptosis

01:20:30.220 --> 01:20:33.560
which is naturally occurring cell
death of that stem cell niche.

01:20:33.560 --> 01:20:36.200
We've been talking a lot about
the antigen or growth phase of hair.

01:20:36.200 --> 01:20:37.960
We also talked about the catagen or

01:20:37.990 --> 01:20:40.320
the recession of that hair
from the inside out.

01:20:40.320 --> 01:20:41.600
But remember that third phase,

01:20:41.600 --> 01:20:45.080
the telogen phase, where that whole bulb
down  at the bottom, the bulge,

01:20:45.080 --> 01:20:47.480
as it's called,
gets pinched off and the whole thing dies

01:20:47.480 --> 01:20:49.680
and takes the stem cells
off to the grave with it.

01:20:49.710 --> 01:20:54.160
It appears that caffeine can offset
the death of that niche and potentially

01:20:54.180 --> 01:20:58.840
maintain  the stem cell population longer,
making caffeine a really good choice

01:20:58.870 --> 01:21:02.360
to think about in conjunction
with  the various chemical treatments

01:21:02.380 --> 01:21:06.680
aimed  at directly attacking the DHT
pathway  that we'll talk about next.

01:21:06.710 --> 01:21:10.440
So there's one very direct way
to increase hair growth and maintain

01:21:10.460 --> 01:21:14.900
the hair  that you  have on your head,
and that's to increase IGF-1.

01:21:14.920 --> 01:21:19.560
That can be accomplished through
prescription drugs such as growth hormone

01:21:19.590 --> 01:21:23.800
and things that stimulate the release
of growth hormone and IGF-1.

01:21:23.800 --> 01:21:25.480
Keep in mind, growth hormone  is released

01:21:25.500 --> 01:21:28.920
from the anterior  pituitary during
the first hours of sleep,

01:21:28.920 --> 01:21:31.640
especially when you haven't eaten
anything  for the two hours prior

01:21:31.670 --> 01:21:35.600
to sleep, and especially  when
you get regular bedtimes.

01:21:35.630 --> 01:21:37.320
Yes, this is a real thing.

01:21:37.340 --> 01:21:41.480
If you are going to sleep at variable
bedtimes, especially if you go to sleep

01:21:41.500 --> 01:21:45.160
much later  than your usual habitual
bedtime, you will miss that growth

01:21:45.180 --> 01:21:49.480
hormone  pulse that normally occurs
in the first 2-3 hours of sleep.

01:21:49.480 --> 01:21:50.760
This does not mean  that you need to be

01:21:50.760 --> 01:21:53.280
neurotic about getting to sleep
at the exact same time every night.

01:21:53.280 --> 01:21:54.880
There's probably  a plus or minus 30-

01:21:54.910 --> 01:21:58.040
minute window,
and it doesn't mean  that you can't stay

01:21:58.070 --> 01:22:02.040
out late or have a bad night's sleep
every once in a while or get woken up.

01:22:02.040 --> 01:22:03.720
Your hair isn't going to fall out.

01:22:03.750 --> 01:22:06.200
My dad's story notwithstanding,

01:22:06.200 --> 01:22:08.280
your hair isn't going to all
fallout because of that.

01:22:08.280 --> 01:22:09.720
But you do want to try and get

01:22:09.720 --> 01:22:11.920
that  natural growth
hormone release each night.

01:22:11.950 --> 01:22:13.360
And as I mentioned,

01:22:13.380 --> 01:22:18.060
there are prescription  approaches
and those are growth hormone itself.

01:22:18.090 --> 01:22:22.120
Things like sermorelin, which is
a peptide that increases growth hormone.

01:22:22.140 --> 01:22:23.920
It's actually a secreted dog.

01:22:23.950 --> 01:22:28.600
It causes the secretion of growth
hormone and thereby increases in IGF-1.

01:22:28.630 --> 01:22:29.840
This is well documented.

01:22:29.870 --> 01:22:34.120
Both growth hormone and IGF-1, as I
mentioned,  are available by prescription.

01:22:34.140 --> 01:22:37.060
They are not without their side effects.

01:22:37.090 --> 01:22:38.960
They do cause growth of all tissues.

01:22:38.990 --> 01:22:42.880
They do increase height in children,
They increase bone mass and density.

01:22:42.910 --> 01:22:46.360
They can increase mainly fat loss,
not so much muscle size,

01:22:46.380 --> 01:22:49.720
but they can increase leanness and they
increase hair growth,

01:22:49.720 --> 01:22:52.840
They can increase turnover of skin,
they can make skin look more youthful.

01:22:52.840 --> 01:22:54.320
All these things sound wonderful.

01:22:54.340 --> 01:22:57.480
And yet they also have problems because

01:22:57.480 --> 01:23:00.960
they can increase  growth of small tumors
that normally might be eliminated.

01:23:00.990 --> 01:23:03.000
So there is an increased cancer risk

01:23:03.030 --> 01:23:08.740
with growth hormone treatments and IGF-1
or anything that increases IGF-1  such as

01:23:08.760 --> 01:23:12.640
sermorelin or ipamorelin, any of the
peptides  that you hear about nowadays.

01:23:12.670 --> 01:23:16.820
That said, a number of people  are using
sermorelin as an indirect way to increase

01:23:16.840 --> 01:23:19.200
IGF-1 and thereby
to increase hair growth.

01:23:19.220 --> 01:23:23.080
It does seem to be fairly effective
in doing that, especially when done

01:23:23.080 --> 01:23:25.240
in conjunction with  other
treatments that we'll talk about.

01:23:25.240 --> 01:23:29.120
But keep in mind, these are prescription
drugs and they do carry their own risks.

01:23:29.140 --> 01:23:33.000
The other thing about stimulating
the natural production of IGF-1 is that,

01:23:33.030 --> 01:23:35.760
as its name suggests,
insulin growth factor one,

01:23:35.790 --> 01:23:39.680
it is insulin dependent in many ways,
if not for its secretion,

01:23:39.710 --> 01:23:43.400
then for its action at the hair
follicle and stem cell.

01:23:43.400 --> 01:23:46.760
So one of the things  you really want
to pay attention to is to avoid being

01:23:46.790 --> 01:23:51.600
insulin resistant, or rather you
want to try  to be insulin sensitive.

01:23:51.600 --> 01:23:52.920
So if you're carrying  a lot of excess

01:23:52.950 --> 01:23:56.520
body fat, if you're obese  or if you have
type two diabetes,

01:23:56.520 --> 01:23:59.200
meaning your insulin resistant,
you're going to want to deal with that.

01:23:59.200 --> 01:24:01.800
There are a number of prescription
treatments to deal with that nowadays.

01:24:01.830 --> 01:24:05.860
People are very excited about all the GLP
one agonists, but in addition to that,

01:24:05.880 --> 01:24:09.240
regular cardiovascular exercise
and resistance exercise,

01:24:09.260 --> 01:24:14.740
making sure that your body fat percentage
is not in excess of where it needs to be.

01:24:14.760 --> 01:24:16.760
Everyone has a slightly different idea

01:24:16.760 --> 01:24:19.200
of where it needs to be,
both cosmetically and for health.

01:24:19.200 --> 01:24:22.920
So that's a conversation between you
and your doctor and you and you frankly.

01:24:22.950 --> 01:24:27.960
But you want to avoid being insulin
resistant because being insulin resistant

01:24:27.990 --> 01:24:30.820
and being obese can
indeed lead to hair loss.

01:24:30.840 --> 01:24:31.960
There are many people out there  who are

01:24:31.990 --> 01:24:36.760
not obese who nonetheless are experiencing
hair thinning and hair loss because they

01:24:36.790 --> 01:24:40.540
are insulin resistant by way
of reduced IGF-1 activity.

01:24:40.560 --> 01:24:42.840
There are a few supplements.
So these are over-the-counter

01:24:42.870 --> 01:24:47.200
supplements  such as myo-i nositol,
taken at dosages of about  900 milligrams

01:24:47.220 --> 01:24:51.400
before  sleep, which by the way,
can also assist in sleep or things like

01:24:51.420 --> 01:24:56.200
berberine or metformin, which are
known  to improve insulin sensitivity.

01:24:56.220 --> 01:25:00.760
Each and every one of these has its own
profile of positive and negative effects.

01:25:00.790 --> 01:25:06.040
The lowest number of side effects  is
associated with 900 milligram myo-i

01:25:06.040 --> 01:25:09.320
nositol  taken about 30 minutes before
sleep, mostly because it can make people

01:25:09.340 --> 01:25:12.560
a little bit drowsy
and it does aid sleep  in some  really

01:25:12.590 --> 01:25:15.480
great ways,
but really exercise and maintaining

01:25:15.480 --> 01:25:18.200
a healthy  nutritional program
are also going to be key.

01:25:18.220 --> 01:25:19.680
You just can't discard those.

01:25:19.680 --> 01:25:21.480
Berberine, which is a substance  made

01:25:21.480 --> 01:25:24.200
from tree bark is sometimes
called  the poor man's metformin.

01:25:24.220 --> 01:25:29.240
Metformin being the equally effective
prescription version of berberine.

01:25:29.240 --> 01:25:30.160
Or put differently,

01:25:30.180 --> 01:25:34.600
berberine is the non-prescription but
equally effective version of metformin.

01:25:34.630 --> 01:25:36.400
Keep in mind that  both berberine

01:25:36.420 --> 01:25:39.520
and metformin dramatically
reduce blood sugar levels.

01:25:39.520 --> 01:25:40.680
And so if you're not going to take  them

01:25:40.680 --> 01:25:43.440
with carbohydrates, it can lead
to some feelings of discomfort.

01:25:43.440 --> 01:25:44.800
That's why I'm not a fan of them.

01:25:44.830 --> 01:25:48.040
But if your goal is to really improve
insulin sensitivity,

01:25:48.070 --> 01:25:52.320
they are considered very potent tools
on the list of things that can do that.

01:25:52.320 --> 01:25:55.120
The other thing that's really important
for maintaining proper hair growth,

01:25:55.140 --> 01:25:58.100
this antigen phase,
is that you need sufficient iron.

01:25:58.130 --> 01:26:01.120
This is because iron and ferritin play

01:26:01.140 --> 01:26:05.800
a key role in the cell growth pathways
that go from the stem cells

01:26:05.830 --> 01:26:08.760
to the stimulation of keratin
within the hair itself.

01:26:08.760 --> 01:26:09.760
I don't have time to go into  this

01:26:09.790 --> 01:26:14.400
pathway in a lot of detail, but you can
have your blood levels  of iron measured.

01:26:14.400 --> 01:26:15.800
This turns out to be pretty important

01:26:15.800 --> 01:26:18.760
because you don't just want to start
popping iron supplements because too much

01:26:18.790 --> 01:26:21.620
iron can be toxic,
too little means you're anemic.

01:26:21.640 --> 01:26:27.360
For women,  the levels of iron  that you
want are somewhere between 25 and 100.

01:26:27.380 --> 01:26:30.220
And for men, somewhere between 30 and 150.

01:26:30.250 --> 01:26:34.320
Fortunately,  the tests or the blood
tests  for iron are usually a very

01:26:34.340 --> 01:26:37.320
inexpensive add to your
current blood panel.

01:26:37.320 --> 01:26:38.680
So if you're going in for a blood panel

01:26:38.710 --> 01:26:42.640
for LDL, HDL, typical things,
or if you're doing the more elaborate

01:26:42.640 --> 01:26:45.200
hormone testing,
which I do recommend people do if they

01:26:45.200 --> 01:26:48.840
can afford it or if their insurance covers
it, do ask for an iron test as well.

01:26:48.840 --> 01:26:51.240
And if your iron is low,
you may need to supplement your iron.

01:26:51.240 --> 01:26:53.640
If your iron is too high,
that's not good either.

01:26:53.670 --> 01:26:56.400
But iron plays a key role in the antigen

01:26:56.400 --> 01:27:00.360
phase of hair growth, so you want to make
sure  you at least have sufficient iron.

01:27:00.360 --> 01:27:01.520
And if you don't, you want to make sure

01:27:01.550 --> 01:27:04.820
that you're getting it from nutrition
and or supplementation.

01:27:04.840 --> 01:27:07.320
Earlier, we were talking
about dihydrotestosterone.

01:27:07.340 --> 01:27:08.520
Dihydrotestosterone,

01:27:08.550 --> 01:27:12.280
just to jog your memory,
is a form of testosterone that combine

01:27:12.300 --> 01:27:17.540
the androgen  receptor at five times
the affinity of regular testosterone.

01:27:17.570 --> 01:27:21.500
Both men and women have a lot
of testosterone relative to estrogen.

01:27:21.520 --> 01:27:25.500
It just so happens that men tend to have
more testosterone than women do overall.

01:27:25.530 --> 01:27:30.440
But both men and women, as they age,
convert more of the testosterone they

01:27:30.460 --> 01:27:35.600
have  to dihydrotestosterone
and dihydrotestosterone does two things

01:27:35.600 --> 01:27:37.960
that are bad  for hair
maintenance and hair growth.

01:27:37.990 --> 01:27:42.180
First of all, it shortens  the antigen
phase, that growth phase.

01:27:42.200 --> 01:27:46.080
Whatever hair is going to grow is going
to occur over a shorter period of time.

01:27:46.110 --> 01:27:48.800
Second of all,  because  of the presence

01:27:48.830 --> 01:27:53.600
of androgen receptors on the stem cell
niche area and around it,

01:27:53.630 --> 01:27:57.460
it actually miniaturize the follicle
and the stem cell niche.

01:27:57.480 --> 01:28:01.040
In other words,  it makes the population
of cells that give rise to more hair

01:28:01.070 --> 01:28:04.760
protein smaller and can
eliminate it altogether.

01:28:04.790 --> 01:28:07.280
And that is why anything  that reduces 5-

01:28:07.300 --> 01:28:13.400
alpha reductase is going to reduce DHT,
is going to maintain or extend the growth

01:28:13.420 --> 01:28:18.120
phase, the antigen phase of hair growth
and is going to offset  or prevent some

01:28:18.150 --> 01:28:23.400
of the telogen phase, the pinching off
and the removal of that stem cell niche.

01:28:23.400 --> 01:28:25.080
Now, one substance that  we know can

01:28:25.110 --> 01:28:29.480
inhibit 5-alpha reductase,
although it does it pretty weakly is saw

01:28:29.500 --> 01:28:32.640
palmetto, which is an extract
of the saw palmetto berry.

01:28:32.640 --> 01:28:35.240
To be honest, I don't know how
this was initially discovered.

01:28:35.240 --> 01:28:37.440
If anyone knows,  please put
it in the show note captions.

01:28:37.460 --> 01:28:41.360
When I looked online I found a bunch
of conflicting stories about who was

01:28:41.380 --> 01:28:46.120
the first person  to start extracting the
extract of the saw palmetto berries.

01:28:46.150 --> 01:28:48.440
So I have no idea
which one of those is true.

01:28:48.460 --> 01:28:50.340
Maybe somebody can tell me.

01:28:50.360 --> 01:28:51.760
The good thing about  saw palmetto

01:28:51.790 --> 01:28:55.760
treatment is that it is known to have
very few,  if any, side effects.

01:28:55.760 --> 01:28:57.000
There might be some side effects

01:28:57.030 --> 01:29:01.540
in about 1% of people, but it's not
associated with a lot of side effects.

01:29:01.570 --> 01:29:04.240
It's also known that when taken  at about

01:29:04.240 --> 01:29:07.400
300 milligrams per day and here it
doesn't  have to be that strict.

01:29:07.420 --> 01:29:12.060
Most of the studies that I explored
involved taking anywhere from  200-

01:29:12.080 --> 01:29:15.200
500 milligrams of saw palmetto,
but most of them focused  on about

01:29:15.230 --> 01:29:19.280
300 milligrams of saw palmetto per day,
divided into two or three doses.

01:29:19.280 --> 01:29:22.260
Why?
Well, it has a relatively short half-life,

01:29:22.280 --> 01:29:25.040
meaning it's going to get cleared
from the bloodstream and more importantly,

01:29:25.040 --> 01:29:27.400
its biological action is
going to be very short-lived.

01:29:27.420 --> 01:29:31.880
So if you can get a hold of  50 or 100-
milligram capsules or tablets

01:29:31.910 --> 01:29:35.720
of saw palmetto and divide those up,
take them in the morning,

01:29:35.720 --> 01:29:38.000
afternoon and evening,
or even just in the morning and evening

01:29:38.030 --> 01:29:41.180
to achieve a total of about
300 milligrams per day.

01:29:41.210 --> 01:29:46.520
That's going to very likely help you hold
on to some of the hair that you would

01:29:46.550 --> 01:29:49.400
have otherwise lost,
maybe even grow some new hair.

01:29:49.420 --> 01:29:53.360
And I say maybe give you  some new hair
growth because  saw palmetto is not

01:29:53.380 --> 01:29:57.680
known  to be a particularly robust
treatment for the reversal of hair loss.

01:29:57.680 --> 01:29:59.160
It's known to have some effect,

01:29:59.190 --> 01:30:02.960
but it's generally taken in conjunction
with a bunch of other things.

01:30:02.990 --> 01:30:07.620
And so it's really hard to tease out
just what amount of hair growth or

01:30:07.650 --> 01:30:10.840
prevention of hair loss is  due
to  saw palmetto specifically.

01:30:10.840 --> 01:30:11.960
But I mention it here  because

01:30:11.990 --> 01:30:15.240
the mechanism of action is logical
and fairly well-known,

01:30:15.270 --> 01:30:20.820
which is this week effect  in reducing 5-
alpha reductase and thereby reducing DHT.

01:30:20.840 --> 01:30:22.680
So again, because it has  relatively low

01:30:22.710 --> 01:30:26.720
side effects, even though it's not super
effective  and because it's fairly low

01:30:26.750 --> 01:30:31.900
cost and it's available over the counter,
I felt it was important to include.

01:30:31.920 --> 01:30:33.860
Now, as soon as people hear things like

01:30:33.880 --> 01:30:36.440
saw palmetto berry, they're probably also
thinking, "Oh boy,

01:30:36.440 --> 01:30:39.920
here comes all the herbals." Now keep
in mind that there are some herbal

01:30:39.950 --> 01:30:42.960
compounds that have pretty
robust biological effects.

01:30:42.990 --> 01:30:47.820
And we talked before in our optimizing
testosterone episodes about things like

01:30:47.840 --> 01:30:52.000
Tongkat Ali and  Fadogia agrestis,
which taken incorrect dosages

01:30:52.000 --> 01:30:54.320
and in the correct way,
can be pretty  potent for increasing

01:30:54.340 --> 01:30:58.040
luteinizing hormone and free
testosterone  that can have huge effects.

01:30:58.040 --> 01:31:01.920
It's not like taking exogenous anabolic
steroids, but they can have real effects.

01:31:01.950 --> 01:31:04.640
And so herbal compounds can be potent.

01:31:04.670 --> 01:31:08.680
However, I do acknowledge that there is
a vast market out there of herbal

01:31:08.710 --> 01:31:12.280
compounds  and plant-based
compounds that people are arguing.

01:31:12.300 --> 01:31:16.020
Mostly the people who sell them are
arguing can increase hair growth.

01:31:16.040 --> 01:31:18.200
There are some decent
studies of these things.

01:31:18.230 --> 01:31:20.480
The hard part about studying these herbal

01:31:20.500 --> 01:31:24.440
compounds and these plant-derived
compounds  for increasing hair growth is

01:31:24.460 --> 01:31:27.400
that they are often taken
in combination with one another.

01:31:27.420 --> 01:31:29.720
In fact,  most of the hair growth

01:31:29.750 --> 01:31:34.880
supplements that involve these herbal
compounds  and plant compounds include 5

01:31:34.910 --> 01:31:37.400
or 10,  sometimes even
more things altogether.

01:31:37.400 --> 01:31:39.120
So teasing out which ones are effective

01:31:39.150 --> 01:31:41.880
and which dosages are effective
is nearly impossible.

01:31:41.880 --> 01:31:43.540
There are just too many variables.

01:31:43.570 --> 01:31:47.560
You will hear, for instance,
that green tea extract, Reishi Mushroom,

01:31:47.590 --> 01:31:53.860
pumpkin oil, zinc, curcumin, all
of these things can increase hair growth.

01:31:53.880 --> 01:31:57.040
Perhaps the only thing on that list
that makes logical sense with respect

01:31:57.070 --> 01:32:01.540
to the biochemistry is that curcumin is
known to, in some people,

01:32:01.570 --> 01:32:06.560
be a potent inhibitor of 5-alpha reductase
and DHD so much so that I can personally

01:32:06.590 --> 01:32:12.800
say for me  I once took curcumin,
turmeric, it's also called in high dosage.

01:32:12.830 --> 01:32:17.100
This is about a gram to 2 gram capsules
and I felt absolutely terrible.

01:32:17.130 --> 01:32:18.280
I mean, just dreadful.

01:32:18.280 --> 01:32:19.640
I don't care if it allowed me  to keep

01:32:19.670 --> 01:32:23.780
my hair forever, I would rather
lose  all my hair three times over.

01:32:23.800 --> 01:32:25.240
I guess that means  it
would have grown back.

01:32:25.270 --> 01:32:26.880
I'd rather lose all my hair.

01:32:26.910 --> 01:32:28.940
Let's just put it that way

01:32:28.960 --> 01:32:32.140
than ever take curcumin or
turmeric in high dosages again.

01:32:32.160 --> 01:32:35.640
In saying that, I know that many people
take turmeric and curcumin and really like

01:32:35.670 --> 01:32:39.440
its anti-inflammatory properties
and don't  experience any side effects.

01:32:39.460 --> 01:32:44.140
I just happen to be particularly sensitive
to curcumin by way of this DHT pathway.

01:32:44.160 --> 01:32:47.200
I know this by way of blood work, so I'm
never going to hear that stuff again.

01:32:47.230 --> 01:32:50.120
That said, a lot of these herbal compounds

01:32:50.150 --> 01:32:55.780
and cocktails probably  will have some
minor marginal,

01:32:55.800 --> 01:32:58.520
infinitesimally small,
somewhere in that range effect

01:32:58.550 --> 01:33:02.920
on maintaining hair growth  or
in stimulating new hair growth.

01:33:02.920 --> 01:33:04.200
It's just that there  really aren't

01:33:04.200 --> 01:33:06.040
clinical studies
to support any one of them.

01:33:06.040 --> 01:33:08.840
And that's why I singled out saw palmetto
as one of the few

01:33:08.870 --> 01:33:12.080
for which the biochemical pathway
of inhibiting 5-alpha reductase

01:33:12.110 --> 01:33:16.200
and the low incidence of side effects
and the fact that many people have used it

01:33:16.230 --> 01:33:19.600
with some degree of success
makes it a standalone.

01:33:19.630 --> 01:33:22.360
I wouldn't say recommendation,
but a consideration.

01:33:22.380 --> 01:33:26.880
Another commonly discussed and use
commercial compound for offsetting hair

01:33:26.910 --> 01:33:29.960
loss and stimulating hair
growth is ketoconazole.

01:33:29.990 --> 01:33:35.240
Sometimes this is known as  Nizoral where
Nizoral is   the brand name of a shampoo.

01:33:35.270 --> 01:33:38.120
Ketoconazole is an antifungal  that was

01:33:38.150 --> 01:33:42.340
initially developed to treat
dandruff  and severe psoriasis.

01:33:42.370 --> 01:33:46.640
Ketoconazole has been shown to be
effective in increasing hair number.

01:33:46.640 --> 01:33:48.440
It's also been shown to be effective

01:33:48.460 --> 01:33:52.200
in increasing hair diameter,
which is somewhat surprising because one

01:33:52.230 --> 01:33:57.400
of the common side effects of ketoconazole
is drying, thinning and brittle hair.

01:33:57.400 --> 01:33:59.600
So what's going on there  is
a little unclear.

01:33:59.600 --> 01:34:01.060
We'll return to that in a moment.

01:34:01.090 --> 01:34:04.320
The mechanism of action
for ketoconazole is pretty interesting.

01:34:04.320 --> 01:34:05.640
Remember earlier we were talking  about

01:34:05.670 --> 01:34:09.300
the sebaceous gland and the production
of sebum,   that oily stuff

01:34:09.330 --> 01:34:12.240
whose very name seems  to evoke
disgust in certain people.

01:34:12.270 --> 01:34:14.520
Well, ketoconazole can disrupt  some

01:34:14.550 --> 01:34:18.760
of the fungal growth that frankly,
we all have on our scalp all the time.

01:34:18.790 --> 01:34:22.760
I know this is a surprise to many of you,
but you are constantly bombarded

01:34:22.790 --> 01:34:26.760
with viruses, bacteria
and funguses all the time.

01:34:26.760 --> 01:34:28.280
But we managed to battle  those off

01:34:28.280 --> 01:34:30.600
with our immune system,
either by physical barriers such as

01:34:30.630 --> 01:34:35.540
an oil barrier like the sebum
or through antimicrobial action.

01:34:35.570 --> 01:34:38.820
Chemical approaches  our immune system,
the sebum, etc,

01:34:38.840 --> 01:34:43.920
ketoconazole acts as an antifungal
that in some way seems to reinforce

01:34:43.950 --> 01:34:48.080
the properties of sebum at keeping
out other fungal infections.

01:34:48.110 --> 01:34:53.360
And the net effect, at least as far as
we know, is a mild reduction in DHT.

01:34:53.380 --> 01:34:55.960
Now exactly how this
happens isn't really clear.

01:34:55.990 --> 01:34:58.200
What is clear is that the use

01:34:58.230 --> 01:35:04.240
of ketoconazole shampoo is
2-4 times per week with a scalp contact

01:35:04.270 --> 01:35:09.920
time of about 3-5 minutes has been shown
to give about an 80%  response rate

01:35:09.950 --> 01:35:12.440
of maintaining  hair
that would otherwise be lost.

01:35:12.460 --> 01:35:14.400
So that's pretty dramatic, 80%.

01:35:14.400 --> 01:35:15.960
What is less clear is  whether or not

01:35:15.990 --> 01:35:19.420
ketoconazole shampoo can actually
stimulate new hair growth.

01:35:19.440 --> 01:35:21.640
But as you're probably  starting
to realize,

01:35:21.670 --> 01:35:25.480
this is always a bit of a tough thing
to disentangle maintenance of hair

01:35:25.480 --> 01:35:27.680
that you would have lost
versus new hair growth.

01:35:27.690 --> 01:35:30.240
Certainly,
that's an easy thing  to disambiguate if

01:35:30.270 --> 01:35:33.460
you have a patch of scalp  where there is
absolutely no hair,

01:35:33.490 --> 01:35:38.080
these so-called dead zones that you
can resurrect with certain treatments.

01:35:38.110 --> 01:35:41.320
But what about areas of your
scalp  where hair is thinning?

01:35:41.320 --> 01:35:43.400
So, for instance, on the top of your head,

01:35:43.420 --> 01:35:46.980
this is where many women will first
experience pattern, hair loss.

01:35:47.000 --> 01:35:50.340
Alopecia is right at their midline,

01:35:50.360 --> 01:35:51.920
especially  if they
have a part right there.

01:35:51.920 --> 01:35:53.280
They'll start to notice that under very

01:35:53.280 --> 01:35:55.160
bright light,
fluorescent lights  in particular,

01:35:55.190 --> 01:35:59.340
they'll notice a thinning  of their
hair there or  in the forehead region.

01:35:59.370 --> 01:36:01.940
They'll start using  ketoconazole shampoo.

01:36:01.960 --> 01:36:06.520
Again, the typical recommendation  is 2-4
times per week with a scalp contact time

01:36:06.520 --> 01:36:09.520
of 3-5 minutes and really rubbing
it in  and then rinsing it out.

01:36:09.520 --> 01:36:12.040
You don't need to be super vigorous,
but you want to make sure  that it gets

01:36:12.040 --> 01:36:15.520
down into the follicle and around
the follicles,  not just sitting on top

01:36:15.550 --> 01:36:18.120
of the hair,
which is going to be especially

01:36:18.150 --> 01:36:21.460
important  for people who have
long hair to really massage it in.

01:36:21.490 --> 01:36:25.440
Well, they will experience a growth
of hair in that particular region

01:36:25.460 --> 01:36:29.120
that almost certainly were due
to miniaturization of the hair follicle

01:36:29.150 --> 01:36:33.520
and reduction of the total population
of stem cells in that follicle as opposed

01:36:33.550 --> 01:36:36.060
to complete  loss
of the stem cell population.

01:36:36.080 --> 01:36:38.960
The reason we say this is that there's no
reason to think that ketoconazole can

01:36:38.990 --> 01:36:42.800
actually stimulate
IGF-1 or activate growth itself.

01:36:42.830 --> 01:36:47.160
It's probably offsetting some
of the reductions in the antigen phase

01:36:47.190 --> 01:36:49.960
and some of the exacerbation
of the telogen phase.

01:36:49.960 --> 01:36:52.040
Now, if you decide to use ketoconazole as

01:36:52.040 --> 01:36:55.360
an approach to offsetting hair loss,
it's very important that  you get a hold

01:36:55.380 --> 01:36:59.400
of a shampoo that's at least 2%
concentration of ketoconazole.

01:36:59.400 --> 01:37:02.840
This is important because a lot
of the ones that are available out there,

01:37:02.870 --> 01:37:05.920
especially online,
are going to be 1% or lower.

01:37:05.950 --> 01:37:10.280
So you want to try and obtain
a ketoconazole shampoo of 2% or higher

01:37:10.300 --> 01:37:14.220
concentration of ketoconazole because
it has other things in it, of course.

01:37:14.240 --> 01:37:17.520
I should mention that there are occasional
side effects with ketoconazole.

01:37:17.520 --> 01:37:21.240
The rates of side effects  from  the meta
analyzes and reviews that I read were

01:37:21.270 --> 01:37:25.000
somewhere between 1% and 8%  of people
will experience some side effects,

01:37:25.030 --> 01:37:27.320
but those side effects
tend to be pretty mild.

01:37:27.340 --> 01:37:29.540
Things like irritation of the scalp,

01:37:29.570 --> 01:37:33.680
things like thinning and brittleness
of the hair that sometimes can be offset

01:37:33.680 --> 01:37:36.200
by using shampoos that  contain
things like biotin.

01:37:36.200 --> 01:37:37.680
I know many people  are probably curious

01:37:37.710 --> 01:37:42.460
about biotin, which is a protein that can
be incorporated into the keratin.

01:37:42.490 --> 01:37:47.200
Whether or not different biotin enriched
shampoos can really enhance the total

01:37:47.230 --> 01:37:50.680
amount of biotin that gets  incorporated
into the hair isn't clear,

01:37:50.710 --> 01:37:54.000
but it is clear that having sufficient
biotin around is important.

01:37:54.030 --> 01:37:56.540
So if you get a little bit extra
from your shampoo,

01:37:56.560 --> 01:38:00.400
you can imagine how that would  "tap
off"  the amount  of biotin in that hair.

01:38:00.400 --> 01:38:01.800
And there are people out there saying

01:38:01.800 --> 01:38:04.720
that by biotin-enriched shampoos
have done wonders for them.

01:38:04.750 --> 01:38:08.140
Who knows?
I'm not going to dispute their experience.

01:38:08.170 --> 01:38:10.280
So if you're going to use ketoconazole,

01:38:10.300 --> 01:38:14.520
keep in mind that the more typical brand
names that are out there,

01:38:14.550 --> 01:38:19.680
you know which ones they are,
oftentimes don't have 2%  or if they do

01:38:19.710 --> 01:38:23.540
have 2%, they can be very drying
and lead to brittle hair.

01:38:23.570 --> 01:38:26.680
There are newer and now fortunately,

01:38:26.710 --> 01:38:29.880
a greater variety of ketoconazole
containing shampoos.

01:38:29.910 --> 01:38:32.200
We as a podcast and I don't have  any

01:38:32.230 --> 01:38:35.600
affiliation to any of these,
but I will provide a links to a couple

01:38:35.630 --> 01:38:40.200
of  the more prominent ones that are known
to have 2% concentration of ketoconazole,

01:38:40.200 --> 01:38:43.320
as well as some other things in them known
to offset some of that dryness

01:38:43.340 --> 01:38:46.700
and brittleness that ketoconazole
shampoos can trigger.

01:38:46.730 --> 01:38:49.080
So by now, I think it will be abundantly

01:38:49.110 --> 01:38:55.080
clear why inhibiting  5-alpha reductase
and thereby reducing DHT should increase

01:38:55.110 --> 01:39:01.740
hair growth because of the negative
impact  that DHT has on the hair follicle.

01:39:01.770 --> 01:39:04.400
The major player in this whole story

01:39:04.420 --> 01:39:09.800
around inhibiting 5-alpha reductase
and reducing DHT to maintain or increase

01:39:09.830 --> 01:39:15.100
hair growth is going to be finasteride
and its close cousin, dutasteride.

01:39:15.130 --> 01:39:19.680
Finasteride is effective in reducing DHT
because of its actions in reducing

01:39:19.710 --> 01:39:24.440
the type two isoenzyme  or
isoform of 5-alpha reductase.

01:39:24.440 --> 01:39:25.800
It turns out there's three different

01:39:25.830 --> 01:39:29.700
isoforms or what are sometimes called
isoenzymes of 5-alpha reductase.

01:39:29.720 --> 01:39:31.820
This is getting pretty
far down in the weeds.

01:39:31.840 --> 01:39:33.160
What I think most of you  just need

01:39:33.190 --> 01:39:38.480
to know is that finasteride reduces DHT,
that's the net product of finasteride

01:39:38.500 --> 01:39:42.180
and in doing so, it can increase
hair count by as much as 20%.

01:39:42.200 --> 01:39:44.060
Pretty remarkable if you think about it.

01:39:44.090 --> 01:39:49.900
In addition, finasteride treatment done
properly, which we'll define in a moment,

01:39:49.920 --> 01:39:54.380
can reduce hair loss in 90%
of all people that take it.

01:39:54.410 --> 01:39:56.560
That is near staggering.

01:39:56.560 --> 01:39:57.840
I mean, there aren't many pharmaceuticals

01:39:57.870 --> 01:40:00.720
Out there that have that
efficacy, really dramatic.

01:40:00.750 --> 01:40:05.720
In addition, it's known to increase hair
thickness by about 20- 30% overall,

01:40:05.750 --> 01:40:10.600
so not just create new growth of hairs,
and thicker hairs, but whatever hair you

01:40:10.600 --> 01:40:13.380
do happen to have on your head,
it can further thicken those.

01:40:13.410 --> 01:40:18.520
The finasteride story is one,
I think, of general success.

01:40:18.550 --> 01:40:20.760
It really seems to improve hair  growth,

01:40:20.790 --> 01:40:23.540
and help you hold  on to
the hair that you have.

01:40:23.570 --> 01:40:25.760
The issue with finasteride is twofold.

01:40:25.770 --> 01:40:29.720
First of all, it is known to have some
pretty significant side effects if it's

01:40:29.750 --> 01:40:34.120
not dosed properly,
and in particular  populations of people.

01:40:34.150 --> 01:40:37.520
This is because there is a wide  variation

01:40:37.550 --> 01:40:42.300
in the amount of the different
Isozymes that people make.

01:40:42.320 --> 01:40:44.480
This is why I brought up
the Isozymes earlier.

01:40:44.500 --> 01:40:49.240
Some people make more of Isozyme one
and three, some people make more of

01:40:49.270 --> 01:40:53.240
Isozyme two and three,
and every variation thereof.

01:40:53.270 --> 01:40:57.840
When people take finasteride,
some people are very strong responders,

01:40:57.870 --> 01:41:01.680
and they achieve really effective
hair regrowth and maintenance of hair.

01:41:01.710 --> 01:41:05.120
Other people less effective,
although still pretty impressive.

01:41:05.150 --> 01:41:07.240
But the catalog of side effects

01:41:07.270 --> 01:41:10.040
that people experience
at a given dose, varies widely.

01:41:10.070 --> 01:41:13.300
There's a lot of trial
and error that has to take place.

01:41:13.330 --> 01:41:17.160
Also, I should point out that finasteride
comes in two major forms.

01:41:17.190 --> 01:41:20.080
There's an oral form
and there's a topical form.

01:41:20.110 --> 01:41:23.700
This is not unlike our
discussion of minoxidil earlier.

01:41:23.730 --> 01:41:26.520
Topical finasteride is typically taken

01:41:26.550 --> 01:41:31.720
in 1% solution or ointment and rubbed
into the head, sometimes it's now also

01:41:31.750 --> 01:41:35.600
incorporated into shampoos,
but typically it's put into a solution

01:41:35.630 --> 01:41:39.560
that people rub into their head,
and it is thought that the 1% solutions

01:41:39.590 --> 01:41:43.940
are equivalent to one mg
of systemic finasteride.

01:41:43.960 --> 01:41:45.680
Now we need to take a step back and ask

01:41:45.680 --> 01:41:47.800
why was finasteride
developed in the first place?

01:41:47.830 --> 01:41:50.280
Well, finasteride, as a fairly potent five

01:41:50.300 --> 01:41:53.740
alpha reductase inhibitor,
it's great at lowering DHT.

01:41:53.770 --> 01:41:55.400
It was developed for treatment

01:41:55.420 --> 01:41:58.920
of prostate enlargement and various
issues  of the prostate that are

01:41:58.950 --> 01:42:01.640
associated with elevated DHT
that occurs with age.

01:42:01.640 --> 01:42:03.480
The topical finasteride were designed

01:42:03.500 --> 01:42:07.440
with the hope that the finasteride would
make it into the hair follicle,

01:42:07.460 --> 01:42:11.080
and would inhibit DHT there  and allow
for more growth of the hair,

01:42:11.080 --> 01:42:13.640
which apparently it does,
but not make it into the systemic

01:42:13.640 --> 01:42:15.520
circulation,
or at least not at concentrations

01:42:15.550 --> 01:42:19.360
sufficient enough to cause as many
side effects as with the oral dosing.

01:42:19.380 --> 01:42:23.700
Now, the problem is,  it does
make it into systemic circulation.

01:42:23.730 --> 01:42:25.360
The issue is also,

01:42:25.380 --> 01:42:30.900
that topical application  of finasteride
is harder  to dose than oral finasteride.

01:42:30.920 --> 01:42:34.280
I'm not saying you should be taking oral
rather than topical finasteride,

01:42:34.300 --> 01:42:38.240
but keep in mind  that the dosages
of finasteride that have been shown to be

01:42:38.270 --> 01:42:41.720
effective for inducing hair  growth,
cover an enormous range.

01:42:41.750 --> 01:42:46.000
As low as 0.01mg per day and as high as

01:42:46.030 --> 01:42:50.960
five mg per day, which is
a just staggering range.

01:42:50.960 --> 01:42:52.920
Now, when trying to simplify the problem

01:42:52.950 --> 01:42:56.360
of how much finasteride to take,
either by way of oral tablet,

01:42:56.380 --> 01:43:01.160
or by way of topical solution,
we can get a bit of leverage on this

01:43:01.190 --> 01:43:05.560
by thinking about how much DHT
reduction occurs as a function of dose.

01:43:05.590 --> 01:43:08.280
There, finasteride shows this really

01:43:08.300 --> 01:43:11.320
interesting, what's called
logarithmic distribution.

01:43:11.340 --> 01:43:12.720
What it means is that,

01:43:12.750 --> 01:43:18.680
for a dosage of 0.01mg of finasteride,
you're going to achieve  approximately

01:43:18.710 --> 01:43:22.760
50% reduction in DHT,
and that's systemic DHT,

01:43:22.790 --> 01:43:28.280
so this is a blood draw   measuring your
DHT, then taking 0.01mg of finasteride.

01:43:28.300 --> 01:43:33.640
Again, 0.01, very low dose of finasteride,
repeated a couple of weeks,

01:43:33.670 --> 01:43:38.540
measure people's DHT in their blood again,
and you see that it's reduced by 50%.

01:43:38.570 --> 01:43:48.360
However, at increasing dosages  of 0.2mg,
one mg,  five mg of oral finasteride per

01:43:48.380 --> 01:43:53.320
day, over the same period of time,
the increase or I should say

01:43:53.340 --> 01:43:57.200
the reduction  in dihydrotestosterone,
doesn't increase linearly.

01:43:57.230 --> 01:44:00.660
It's not that you go from 50%-6 0%-75%-

01:44:00.690 --> 01:44:04.880
100% with each increasing dose,
it tapers off, it flattens out.

01:44:04.880 --> 01:44:06.080
It tends to increase a little bit,

01:44:06.110 --> 01:44:12.720
but it's a gradual slope  increasing
as you head from 0.2mg out to five mg.

01:44:12.750 --> 01:44:18.840
What this means is that given
that reducing DHT can cause various side

01:44:18.870 --> 01:44:23.400
effects, sexual side effects,
reductions in either sexual function or

01:44:23.420 --> 01:44:26.920
sexual drive, as well as overall drive
and motivation,

01:44:26.950 --> 01:44:32.160
sometimes even some depressive symptoms
that everything points to taking

01:44:32.190 --> 01:44:36.520
the lowest effective dose of finasteride
and starting with a very low dose

01:44:36.550 --> 01:44:42.320
of finasteride because low doses
of finasteride, even at that 0.01mg taken

01:44:42.340 --> 01:44:47.320
orally daily,
are already leading to a 50%  reduction

01:44:47.340 --> 01:44:51.320
in dihydrotestosterone and thereby taken
for a long  enough period of time,

01:44:51.340 --> 01:44:54.060
should offset hair loss
and stimulate hair growth.

01:44:54.090 --> 01:44:55.600
One of the problems, however,

01:44:55.630 --> 01:45:00.600
is that people will start taking
finasteride at a low dose 0.1mg or 0.2mg,

01:45:00.630 --> 01:45:05.200
maybe even 0.01mg,
and there will be a reduction  in their

01:45:05.230 --> 01:45:09.720
DHT, but because of the long duration
of that antigen phase,

01:45:09.750 --> 01:45:14.000
they don't see a lot of change  in hair
growth in the first month or even two

01:45:14.000 --> 01:45:17.400
months, and so what they end up doing  is
increasing their dosage and then they

01:45:17.420 --> 01:45:21.320
start to see hair growth, but then they
start to experience more side effects.

01:45:21.320 --> 01:45:23.200
Now the side effects of oral finasteride

01:45:23.230 --> 01:45:26.640
are serious enough and common enough
in people that take finasteride

01:45:26.640 --> 01:45:30.320
that the topical solutions were developed,
but there are two one needs to exercise

01:45:30.340 --> 01:45:34.560
caution because if we are going
to translate between topical finasteride

01:45:34.590 --> 01:45:37.520
and oral  finasteride,
with the understanding that topical

01:45:37.550 --> 01:45:40.720
finasteride can actually make it
into the systemic circulation,

01:45:40.720 --> 01:45:43.440
we need to look at what's been shown
in clinical studies,

01:45:43.460 --> 01:45:48.800
which is that for instance,
taking one ml of 0.25% finasteride applied

01:45:48.830 --> 01:45:53.840
to the scalp, this is a very typical
recommendation, translates to the same

01:45:53.870 --> 01:45:59.680
thing  that would be achieved
with 2.5mg of oral finasteride.

01:45:59.680 --> 01:46:01.400
When I say translates to the same thing,

01:46:01.420 --> 01:46:04.980
what I mean is it leads  to the same
concentrations in the blood.

01:46:05.000 --> 01:46:10.660
Now consider that 0.2mg, 0.2mg

01:46:10.690 --> 01:46:14.720
of finasteride in the blood is known
to be effective  in generating new hair

01:46:14.750 --> 01:46:18.660
growth and maintaining hair that one
already has when they start the treatment.

01:46:18.690 --> 01:46:20.960
If you think that the topical

01:46:20.990 --> 01:46:26.440
finasterides are actually creating lower
overall systemic concentrations

01:46:26.460 --> 01:46:29.240
of finasteride, that is
not necessarily the case.

01:46:29.270 --> 01:46:31.880
Again, one ml of topical  finasteride

01:46:31.910 --> 01:46:38.680
at 0.25% leads to a 2.5mg concentration
in the blood, when the effective dose

01:46:38.710 --> 01:46:44.340
within the bloodstream by taking it orally
as a pill is 0.2mg.

01:46:44.360 --> 01:46:47.920
That might not seem like a big deal
to you, although it is a big deal, right?

01:46:47.950 --> 01:46:51.020
We're talking 2.5mg versus 0.2,

01:46:51.050 --> 01:46:55.760
but it is a huge deal when you consider
that the side effects of finasteride

01:46:55.790 --> 01:46:59.900
increase as you increase the concentration
of finasteride in the bloodstream.

01:46:59.920 --> 01:47:01.480
Where does this leave us?

01:47:01.500 --> 01:47:05.600
Should people who are interested
in taking finasteride take the oral form

01:47:05.630 --> 01:47:10.760
at low dose or take the topical form
and simply try and apply it less often or

01:47:10.760 --> 01:47:13.560
guess at what their  systemic
concentration  of finasteride is.

01:47:13.560 --> 01:47:15.480
Well, it's going to vary
from person to person.

01:47:15.480 --> 01:47:18.960
Some people are very sensitive
to finasteride and not in the good sense.

01:47:18.960 --> 01:47:22.360
The side effects just really show up
quickly and they tend to be dramatic.

01:47:22.380 --> 01:47:25.020
Other people, not so much.

01:47:25.040 --> 01:47:28.760
The dosage recommendations  that I was
able to arrive at based on the clinical

01:47:28.790 --> 01:47:32.840
studies and frankly in discussion
with some doctors who prescribe

01:47:32.870 --> 01:47:39.920
finasteride were the following: 0.5mg
to one mg of finasteride as a tablet per

01:47:39.950 --> 01:47:46.040
day seems to be an effective and pretty
safe starting place for most people.

01:47:46.040 --> 01:47:47.560
Now some people will find that even

01:47:47.560 --> 01:47:51.480
that 0.5mg dosage is just going to cause
side effects that are not going to work

01:47:51.500 --> 01:47:56.160
for them, and they're going to either have
to reduce their dosage of finasteride or

01:47:56.190 --> 01:47:59.600
move  to the topical or maybe cease
taking finasteride altogether.

01:47:59.630 --> 01:48:03.780
But for many people out there,
that's going to be pretty well tolerated.

01:48:03.800 --> 01:48:07.400
The key thing here is that one is going
to have to wait some period of time

01:48:07.400 --> 01:48:09.440
to see whether or not
any hair growth occurs.

01:48:09.460 --> 01:48:13.920
It is a naive and frankly  foolish
approach based on what we know about

01:48:13.950 --> 01:48:17.720
the duration of that antigen phase
of the hair to do one of these

01:48:17.720 --> 01:48:20.720
treatments, wait a week or two
and then decide to up your dose.

01:48:20.750 --> 01:48:23.000
Now, it is not foolish to reduce your dose

01:48:23.030 --> 01:48:27.240
if you're experiencing bad side effects,
but to simply increase your dose because

01:48:27.240 --> 01:48:30.800
you're not getting results quickly enough,
that's not going to be  the best approach.

01:48:30.800 --> 01:48:34.000
I really encourage people who are going
to explore the finasteride route,

01:48:34.030 --> 01:48:38.700
to think of this as a long-term project
and to really ratchet up slowly if at all,

01:48:38.720 --> 01:48:41.480
starting initially with a low dose taken
for a long period of time,

01:48:41.500 --> 01:48:46.080
maybe even as long as  25 weeks before
considering going up any further.

01:48:46.080 --> 01:48:49.140
Certainly, as I mentioned before,
if you need to go down further,

01:48:49.170 --> 01:48:53.640
that's not going to be a problem,
at least not in terms  of reducing side

01:48:53.640 --> 01:48:55.360
effects, you're not going to get
additional hair growth,

01:48:55.360 --> 01:48:58.960
but you're certainly not going to increase
your side effects if you reduce your dose.

01:48:58.960 --> 01:49:02.160
However, I will talk a little bit later
about post-finasteride syndrome,

01:49:02.160 --> 01:49:04.480
which is something that's getting
increasing attention nowadays.

01:49:04.480 --> 01:49:06.000
That's something that occurs  after

01:49:06.000 --> 01:49:08.920
people have taken finasteride
for an extended period of time.

01:49:08.920 --> 01:49:11.920
Now some of you have perhaps heard
and I'll just tell you right here,

01:49:11.950 --> 01:49:17.280
that the topical forms of finasteride are
associated with far less side effects.

01:49:17.300 --> 01:49:21.360
Now that might come as surprising given
that topical application of finasteride

01:49:21.380 --> 01:49:23.840
can lead to systemic
distribution of finasteride.

01:49:23.870 --> 01:49:25.920
But the numbers that are out there right

01:49:25.950 --> 01:49:31.160
now, it's that topical finasteride  is
associated with 30-50% fewer side effects

01:49:31.190 --> 01:49:36.140
or 30-5 0% less severe side
effects  than oral finasteride.

01:49:36.160 --> 01:49:38.440
There are several things
probably responsible for that.

01:49:38.440 --> 01:49:40.040
One is that people tend to ratchet up

01:49:40.040 --> 01:49:42.040
their dose of oral
finasteride  pretty quickly.

01:49:42.070 --> 01:49:48.020
But keep in mind that the effective dose
of finasteride in the blood is 0.2mg.

01:49:48.050 --> 01:49:53.000
Earlier I said the typical topical
finasteride solutions are 0.25%. People

01:49:53.030 --> 01:49:55.960
are taking one ml of it,
that equates to 2.5mg,

01:49:55.990 --> 01:50:00.600
and so it seems like a massive overdosing
but here's the discrepancy and here's

01:50:00.630 --> 01:50:04.220
where we can arrive at some
reasonable recommendations.

01:50:04.250 --> 01:50:08.500
If you decide that finasteride is
right for you, you get a prescription.

01:50:08.520 --> 01:50:11.880
I would hope that you're monitoring your
DHT levels and other hormone levels

01:50:11.910 --> 01:50:15.980
that would be ideal,
and working with a doctor, please.

01:50:16.000 --> 01:50:19.600
0.5mg to one mg per day of oral

01:50:19.630 --> 01:50:24.260
finasteride seems to be
the best starting place.

01:50:24.290 --> 01:50:26.260
For topical finasteride.

01:50:26.290 --> 01:50:32.160
It's going to be that one ml of 0.25%
that we talked about earlier,

01:50:32.160 --> 01:50:36.000
but that's taken only one time per week,
and you can fully expect that right after

01:50:36.000 --> 01:50:39.720
the application you will have higher
levels of finasteride in your bloodstream,

01:50:39.750 --> 01:50:44.280
and therefore lower levels of DHT
and that will alter across the week.

01:50:44.280 --> 01:50:45.840
Most people are not going to be able

01:50:45.870 --> 01:50:48.960
to measure their DHT on a day
by day or even weekly basis.

01:50:48.990 --> 01:50:51.560
It's just too expensive
and labor intensive.

01:50:51.560 --> 01:50:53.480
But I think those dosing regimens ought

01:50:53.500 --> 01:50:57.880
to get people into more or less the same
category of optimizing hair maintenance

01:50:57.910 --> 01:51:01.120
and hair growth while minimizing
finasteride side effects.

01:51:01.150 --> 01:51:07.240
One point about finasteride  taken either
alone or in combination is that in recent

01:51:07.270 --> 01:51:11.960
years,  really in the last five or so
years, there's been increasing discussion

01:51:11.990 --> 01:51:14.940
about so-called  post-
finasteride syndrome.

01:51:14.960 --> 01:51:19.440
Now post-finasteride syndrome is indeed
a new phenomenon in the sense

01:51:19.460 --> 01:51:23.480
that finasteride  has been prescribed
for a very long period of time

01:51:23.500 --> 01:51:28.380
for treatment of the prostate,
at dosages of about five mg per day.

01:51:28.410 --> 01:51:29.840
That's a very high dose.

01:51:29.870 --> 01:51:35.280
Sometimes lower,  but as high as five mg
per day, and for many years there was no

01:51:35.300 --> 01:51:37.760
discussion about this
post-finasteride syndrome.

01:51:37.760 --> 01:51:39.460
What is post-finasteride syndrome?

01:51:39.490 --> 01:51:42.800
Post-finasteride syndrome is
when typically it's males.

01:51:42.800 --> 01:51:44.280
This is where it's been described.

01:51:44.300 --> 01:51:50.160
We'll take finasteride at any range
of dosages, from 1mg to 5mg per day.

01:51:50.160 --> 01:51:54.120
They're either doing this for prostate or
more likely they're doing it to offset

01:51:54.150 --> 01:51:57.920
hair loss and increase hair growth,
and then they stop taking finasteride

01:51:57.920 --> 01:52:00.440
for whatever reason,
financial or it wasn't working for them

01:52:00.460 --> 01:52:05.480
or the side effects  were not to their
liking, and they start to experience  some

01:52:05.500 --> 01:52:09.080
very severe what can only be called
syndrome effects,

01:52:09.110 --> 01:52:15.160
such as very reduced libido,
very reduced erectile function,

01:52:15.190 --> 01:52:19.600
very reduced mood to the point
of depression, even suicidal depression.

01:52:19.630 --> 01:52:23.360
This is pretty scary stuff,
especially since it's occurring at an age

01:52:23.360 --> 01:52:26.240
when most of these things are
not typically occurring in males.

01:52:26.260 --> 01:52:28.260
They can occur,  but they're not typical

01:52:28.290 --> 01:52:31.520
of younger males in their
20s and 30s and early 40s.

01:52:31.520 --> 01:52:33.320
We have to ask ourselves
what's going on here?

01:52:33.320 --> 01:52:37.200
After all, people have taken  finasteride
for the prostate at fairly high dosages

01:52:37.200 --> 01:52:39.920
without this post-finasteride
syndrome when they've stopped.

01:52:39.920 --> 01:52:41.520
Now these young males are taking

01:52:41.520 --> 01:52:43.120
finasteride,
they're coming off finasteride

01:52:43.140 --> 01:52:47.240
and they're getting this very severe, very
debilitating  post-finasteride syndrome.

01:52:47.270 --> 01:52:49.160
This has become a hot topic,

01:52:49.160 --> 01:52:52.760
enough so that medical doctors who have
been prescribing finasteride for a very

01:52:52.760 --> 01:52:54.880
long  time, have been
forced to address this.

01:52:54.880 --> 01:52:56.480
I think at first they were  perplexed

01:52:56.480 --> 01:52:59.420
and thought, I don't know, this might
be psychosomatic, whatever that means.

01:52:59.440 --> 01:53:01.480
As a neuroscientist who works on mind-body

01:53:01.500 --> 01:53:04.360
connection, we know that nothing
is truly psychosomatic.

01:53:04.380 --> 01:53:06.440
Everything is of the mind and body.

01:53:06.460 --> 01:53:10.080
But the point is that enough medical
attention has been placed on post-

01:53:10.110 --> 01:53:13.920
finasteride syndrome and trying
to unravel  exactly what that is.

01:53:13.950 --> 01:53:18.520
Where there are now a few general
conclusions about what might be going on.

01:53:18.550 --> 01:53:21.640
First of all, it seems that younger males

01:53:21.670 --> 01:53:25.920
taking finasteride in particular high
dosages to improve hair growth or offset

01:53:25.950 --> 01:53:28.880
hair loss seems to be
one of the key variables.

01:53:28.910 --> 01:53:33.040
We're not seeing this  post-finasteride
syndrome as much in older males.

01:53:33.070 --> 01:53:35.880
In fact, it seems to occur more  in males

01:53:35.910 --> 01:53:39.120
in their 20s and 30s than
males in their 40s and older.

01:53:39.150 --> 01:53:43.880
One thing and it may relate to the ways
in which Dihydrotestosterone, we know,

01:53:43.910 --> 01:53:47.240
has a very key role in early
embryonic development.

01:53:47.270 --> 01:53:50.040
It's actually what's responsible
for the male genitalia.

01:53:50.040 --> 01:53:51.880
It's also responsible for certain things

01:53:51.910 --> 01:53:54.200
in female development,
but mainly in utero,

01:53:54.200 --> 01:53:57.680
it's responsible for male development and
development of the penis in particular.

01:53:57.710 --> 01:53:59.840
Then around the time of puberty,

01:53:59.870 --> 01:54:05.420
Dihydrotestosterone acts again,
in what's called its activating effects

01:54:05.450 --> 01:54:09.920
to further increase growth
of the genitalia, increase the musculature

01:54:09.920 --> 01:54:13.280
bone growth, et cetera, and increase
libido  and a number of other things.

01:54:13.280 --> 01:54:16.040
It's probably also involved
in the activation of puberty.

01:54:16.040 --> 01:54:19.440
It's certainly not the only hormone
involved in the activation of male

01:54:19.440 --> 01:54:21.860
puberty but it's certainly
one of the key players.

01:54:21.880 --> 01:54:26.320
Dihydrotestosterone has these known early
roles in embryonic development

01:54:26.340 --> 01:54:30.440
and in puberty, but what post-finasteride
syndrome seems to indicate is

01:54:30.460 --> 01:54:35.360
that Dihydrotestosterone is likely having
further effects  on male maturation,

01:54:35.380 --> 01:54:38.440
in particular,
maturation of the hypothalamus in areas

01:54:38.460 --> 01:54:43.240
of the brain that continue well
into one's 20s and maybe even one's 30s.

01:54:43.270 --> 01:54:45.480
Here I just want everyone to keep in mind

01:54:45.500 --> 01:54:51.920
that we tend to think about development as
childhood, teenage years, young adulthood,

01:54:51.950 --> 01:54:54.320
adulthood, but really
development never stops.

01:54:54.320 --> 01:54:55.760
Development is something that starts

01:54:55.790 --> 01:54:59.480
at conception and birth, of course,
and then extends all the way out

01:54:59.480 --> 01:55:02.760
until the point when we die,
so even if we live to be in our late 90s

01:55:02.790 --> 01:55:06.720
or achieve 100 years of age,
development is occurring that entire time,

01:55:06.720 --> 01:55:09.880
and these different hormones such as
Dihydrotestosterone are having different

01:55:09.910 --> 01:55:14.840
impact for across the lifespan  and
in different ways across the lifespan.

01:55:14.870 --> 01:55:19.520
There isn't a clear conclusion about what
post-finasteride syndrome is really all

01:55:19.550 --> 01:55:22.880
about, but it points to the fact
that DHT is likely to be involved

01:55:22.910 --> 01:55:27.560
in development of the brain and the brain
to genital axis,

01:55:27.560 --> 01:55:30.260
because I mentioned that because so many
of the side effects

01:55:30.280 --> 01:55:33.320
that are associated with this
post-finasteride syndrome seem to center

01:55:33.320 --> 01:55:36.540
on sexual side effects, although there
are  also the depressive side effects.

01:55:36.560 --> 01:55:39.480
Of course, those can be related
to one another in either direction.

01:55:39.500 --> 01:55:42.240
While I do understand that loss  of one's

01:55:42.270 --> 01:55:46.800
hair, or potential loss of one's hair can
be particularly troubling and anxiety-

01:55:46.830 --> 01:55:50.460
provoking, even cause depression
in some cases, I am sensitive to that.

01:55:50.480 --> 01:55:53.880
You also want to be sensitive
to the fact that some of these treatments,

01:55:53.910 --> 01:55:57.160
such as finasteride,
can carry very serious side effects even

01:55:57.190 --> 01:56:00.740
if you come off them AKA
post-finasteride syndrome.

01:56:00.770 --> 01:56:05.000
As long as we're talking about finasteride
and this general pathway of 5α-Reductase

01:56:05.030 --> 01:56:09.440
inhibition and thereby DHT  inhibition
and on and on topics and themes

01:56:09.460 --> 01:56:15.540
and nomenclature you are now very familiar
with, we have to talk about dutasteride.

01:56:15.570 --> 01:56:19.560
Dutasteride is yet another molecule
similar to finasteride,

01:56:19.590 --> 01:56:23.580
but remember those three isoforms
of the  5α-Reductase enzyme?

01:56:23.610 --> 01:56:25.800
Well, it inhibits all three,

01:56:25.830 --> 01:56:30.820
mainly type one and type two,  but also
type three, and it does it very potently.

01:56:30.840 --> 01:56:35.700
As a consequence,
the typical dosage of oral d utasteride,

01:56:35.730 --> 01:56:44.200
get this, 0.5mg to 2.5mg taken orally,
works 2-5 times faster than typical

01:56:44.230 --> 01:56:52.200
finasteride at inducing hair regrowth
and reduces DHT by, get this, 95%.

01:56:52.230 --> 01:56:57.120
It's just near flatlines DHT,
and that can occur  at concentrations as

01:56:57.150 --> 01:57:02.100
low as 0.5mg, although you will see
prescriptions and people taking d

01:57:02.130 --> 01:57:06.160
utasteride anywhere from 0.5 mg
all the way to 2.5mg orally.

01:57:06.190 --> 01:57:07.980
Now, not surprisingly,

01:57:08.000 --> 01:57:12.240
dutasteride is associated with a lot of
side effects related to the DHT pathway.

01:57:12.270 --> 01:57:14.320
Things like reduction in sex drive,

01:57:14.340 --> 01:57:19.440
reduction in overall drive,
it also tends to impact other hormone

01:57:19.440 --> 01:57:21.720
pathways, so it increases
in estrogen prolactin.

01:57:21.750 --> 01:57:23.860
That's why gynecomastia,

01:57:23.880 --> 01:57:27.480
growth of male breast tissue  sometimes
occurs when people take dutasteride and so

01:57:27.480 --> 01:57:30.240
you're probably asking,
why would anyone take dutasteride?

01:57:30.270 --> 01:57:33.480
Why not just take finasteride
and wait for that hair growth?

01:57:33.480 --> 01:57:34.500
Well,

01:57:34.530 --> 01:57:38.300
the answer is that people are often very
impatient, and it turns out that d

01:57:38.330 --> 01:57:42.600
utasteride  works, about 2-5
times faster than finasteride.

01:57:42.630 --> 01:57:45.240
Some people don't want to wait  a full 30

01:57:45.270 --> 01:57:49.000
weeks or 40 weeks or 50 weeks or more
in order to grow their hair back,

01:57:49.000 --> 01:57:51.320
and they're very concerned about
the hair loss that's occurring.

01:57:51.340 --> 01:57:56.540
They will take what I hope would
be a very low dose of dutasteride.

01:57:56.570 --> 01:57:58.160
I realize that there are ways

01:57:58.190 --> 01:58:02.160
to take dutasteride  that can be safer,
off set some of these side effects.

01:58:02.190 --> 01:58:07.040
But by my read of the literature,
if one is going to try to mildly inhibit

01:58:07.070 --> 01:58:11.920
the DHT pathway, things like saw palmetto,
things like topical caffeine,

01:58:11.920 --> 01:58:15.640
which has some effect  on the androgen
pathway, but as we talked about earlier,

01:58:15.670 --> 01:58:19.040
tickles other pathways,
things like ketoconazole,

01:58:19.070 --> 01:58:23.160
mild reduction in androgen receptor
pathways in the follicle and very direct

01:58:23.160 --> 01:58:24.640
because it's applied
directly to the scalp.

01:58:24.640 --> 01:58:26.200
Things like that are going to be the best

01:58:26.230 --> 01:58:31.560
route for mild reductions in DHT as
an attempt  to maintain hair or grow hair.

01:58:31.590 --> 01:58:36.000
Whereas if one really wants a potent
stimulus for increasing hair growth,

01:58:36.030 --> 01:58:40.120
that's very likely  going to be
finasteride, and hopefully low enough

01:58:40.150 --> 01:58:46.600
dosages of finasteride and hopefully
a patient enough patient person that they

01:58:46.600 --> 01:58:50.400
are  willing to wait the duration of time
required for that hair growth to come back

01:58:50.420 --> 01:58:53.680
because they understand that their
antigen phase takes some time.

01:58:53.680 --> 01:58:55.600
Now the holy grail of all this hair stuff

01:58:55.630 --> 01:59:00.480
is in understanding that no one specific
treatment is magic, and in fact,

01:59:00.500 --> 01:59:04.200
there are now a number of good meta-
analysis comparing  the various

01:59:04.200 --> 01:59:06.960
treatments we've talked about
today alone or in combination.

01:59:06.990 --> 01:59:11.240
We can summarize that pretty easily
by saying that combination treatments

01:59:11.270 --> 01:59:16.680
that involve a mechanical stimulus
and a chemical stimulus are always going

01:59:16.680 --> 01:59:19.920
to be better  than either one alone,
and within the mechanical category,

01:59:19.950 --> 01:59:23.560
the stimulus that seems
to work best is microneedling.

01:59:23.590 --> 01:59:27.600
The combination  of microneedling
and finasteride, can lead to some pretty

01:59:27.630 --> 01:59:31.660
robust  and impressive hair regrowth,
so much so that people that were...

01:59:31.690 --> 01:59:34.080
I would only describe them as pretty bald

01:59:34.110 --> 01:59:37.000
or bald, can regrow
significant amounts of hair.

01:59:37.020 --> 01:59:38.720
I've never seen examples of people

01:59:38.750 --> 01:59:42.560
who were completely bald,
meaning lacking all scalp hair to grow

01:59:42.560 --> 01:59:45.600
back a full head of hair,
but the combination  of microneedling

01:59:45.630 --> 01:59:49.000
and finasteride is probably
the most effective way to go.

01:59:49.000 --> 01:59:51.720
If you're going to do that,
there's no reason why you couldn't also

01:59:51.750 --> 01:59:55.560
use ketoconazole shampoo,
could also use saw palmetto.

01:59:55.560 --> 01:59:58.200
There's no reason to think that these
things collide with one another,

01:59:58.230 --> 02:00:02.040
although anytime you're inhibiting a DHT
pathway, or whether or not you're

02:00:02.040 --> 02:00:04.760
increasing or decreasing any hormone
pathway for that matter,

02:00:04.760 --> 02:00:07.840
you want to be careful about layering
in too many different treatments because

02:00:07.870 --> 02:00:10.080
you don't want your DHT
level to go too low.

02:00:10.080 --> 02:00:14.040
Let's keep in mind that even if you take
a very low dose of finasteride and reduce

02:00:14.070 --> 02:00:17.520
your DHT and don't have side effects,
maybe just the mere addition of

02:00:17.550 --> 02:00:22.240
saw palmetto, which leads to a slight
reduction in DHT combined with some

02:00:22.240 --> 02:00:24.360
caffeine ointment,
would be sufficient enough to start

02:00:24.380 --> 02:00:27.560
inducing some of the  low
DHT associated side effects.

02:00:27.590 --> 02:00:29.360
You really have to see for you,

02:00:29.360 --> 02:00:32.640
and that's one of the major issues
in this whole field  of hair growth

02:00:32.670 --> 02:00:36.960
and regrowth is  that people are highly
individual in their response,

02:00:36.990 --> 02:00:40.000
and in their side effect profile
to these various treatments.

02:00:40.000 --> 02:00:41.200
There's an enormous range there

02:00:41.230 --> 02:00:45.840
and unfortunately, there's no way to know
a priori before doing these treatments

02:00:45.860 --> 02:00:48.760
what your response is going
to be in terms of side effects.

02:00:48.760 --> 02:00:51.360
You're simply going to have to explore,
and I would hope that you would explore

02:00:51.380 --> 02:00:54.560
starting with minimal,
possible effective dosages,

02:00:54.560 --> 02:00:57.320
and to do  that in coordination
with a medical professional so you could

02:00:57.320 --> 02:01:00.920
really evaluate these things that the
level of blood, and cosmetic changes.

02:01:00.950 --> 02:01:03.040
In fact, that's a pretty good motivator

02:01:03.040 --> 02:01:05.640
for thinking about the different
treatments that we talked about today.

02:01:05.670 --> 02:01:08.260
Everything from mechanical treatments,

02:01:08.280 --> 02:01:10.440
as simple as massage,
which we've all heard about,

02:01:10.440 --> 02:01:13.680
but for which there really aren't a lot
of data for supporting hair growth.

02:01:13.710 --> 02:01:17.680
But certainly things like microneedling,
which is a mechanical stimulus

02:01:17.710 --> 02:01:21.460
for which there are pretty good data
that it can improve hair growth.

02:01:21.490 --> 02:01:25.780
Also things like saw palmetto,
a weak DHT antagonist.

02:01:25.800 --> 02:01:30.440
Also things like ketoconazole shampoo,
which again is a weak DHT antagonist

02:01:30.460 --> 02:01:34.200
and operates through some other pathways
as well to stimulate hair growth.

02:01:34.230 --> 02:01:36.600
My suggestion is that anyone  young, old,

02:01:36.630 --> 02:01:40.860
male, female, who's thinking about
embarking  on various treatments for

02:01:40.880 --> 02:01:44.360
offsetting hair loss and stimulating hair
growth, consider both mechanical

02:01:44.380 --> 02:01:47.960
approaches, and the approaches that attack
the chemical pathways,

02:01:47.990 --> 02:01:53.340
that can stimulate  hair growth, and can
inhibit the inhibitors of hair growth.

02:01:53.360 --> 02:01:57.080
In fact, that's the reason why we spend so
much time on the biology of hair growth

02:01:57.110 --> 02:02:00.800
and what shuts down hair growth  early
on in today's episode,

